ent authority and forbid even declared ambient contexts when profile/policy disallows them. Positive output witness: Ambient declaration and profile/policy admission or denial before the authority-bearing operation. Concrete negative case: Undeclared ambient filesystem/network/secret authority is used, or a forbidden profile accepts even a declared ambient context. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types5-integrate-typed-core supplies Actual typed core, ownership/layout and source-origin facts; effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects5-integrate-checked-core-consumers supplies Actual propagated effects and required capability facts; auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/bind-compiler-decisions-to-runtimebuild-enforcement-hooks supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-safe-code-classification-and-taintunsafe-boundaries supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred. Allocation interface/safety/safe10/attenuation (Open). Role: auth owning producer or consuming-boundary checker. Input: authority-bearing operation with separately typed requirements, grants, provider, scope and phase. Required positive predicate: Narrow capability scope/lifetime only, recording parent/derived identity and never adding authority where attenuation i