     "- [ ] `build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-projectlock-normalization-and-constraint-resolution` Implement project/lock normalization and constraint resolution\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Package report](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/bootstrap_impl/components/foundation/00569-stage0-compiled-plan-package-report.clj)\n\nClosing evidence: Real dependency resolution with conflict, profile and capability rejection. Apply declared yank/revocation policy to selection and installation; retain signature/revocation status in locked records and explain each policy decision without silently replacing or erasing locked history. Reject revoked packages unless policy explicitly permits historical rebuild, and report revoked/yanked rejection with PKG5006. For [SAFE14](../../docs/phase-02-safety/043-safe14-supply-chain-safety.md), reject conflicting package safety manifests before compiling dependents; require safe/release locks and validate native source/digest/ABI/target/link/license/wrapper/capability metadata. Compute and present transitive authority diffs including build/runtime, unsafe, plugins, model/tool/secret and generated artifacts; dependency updates cannot silently expand grants. Caller policy checks unsafe summaries, expired reviews and safe exported wrappers/certificates. Apply advisory affected/patched-version, compatibility and capability policy at selection and installation. Reject policy violations without granting undeclared authority. Preserve existing reproducible locks and historical artifacts unless explicit emergency policy applies. Apply yank/revocation, advisory affected/patched versions, compatibility metadata and capability policy at both selection and installation before use. Preserve reproducible existing locks and historical artifacts unless an explicit emergency policy applies; selection never grants undeclared authority. The historical line112 visibility citation remains preserved as metadata-consumer evidence; corrected line110 supplies the policy predicate under the accepted source-role composition. Reject active-policy violations, hidden authority expansion, unreviewed emergency lock changes and silent replacement/erasure of locked history. A complete advisory payload and accountable emergency decision are inputs; resolver output cannot fabricate either. Criterion behavior/pkg1/project-authority-request-check: accept Normalize distinct effect requests, capability requests and explicit denials without adding a deployment grant. Reject A dependency-only request or project declaration silently grants authority or overrides an explicit denial. Emit Effect request table, capability request/deny table, capability diff and PKG1005 with manifest/key/package context. Dependencies: L6, L15, PKG6. Criterion behavior/pkg1/project-dependency-source-check: accept Resolve a declared registry or granted local path and retain its selected source and provenance. Reject A dependency comes from an undeclared registry or ungranted local path, including generated-source roots without traceable provenance. Emit Normalized dependency root set and source decision with PKG1004. Dependencies: PKG4, PKG5, PKG9. Criterion behavior/pkg1/project-normalization: accept Parse EDN-like project data offline without macro expansion or execution and emit a deterministic canonical manifest/hash containing explicit package/version/edition/compiler/roots/profiles/targets/entrypoints/dependencies/effects/capabilities/tasks/unsafe/artifact/signing/reproducibility/provenance declarations. Reject Reading configuration requires execution; a required field or planned artifact kind is absent; a generated root lacks its generated/provenance declaration. Emit Normalized manifest/hash, root and target sets, request tables, unsafe summary, graph seeds, emission plan and release-policy inputs; PKG1001/PKG1008. Dependencies: PKG1, S3, S9. Criterion behavior/pkg1/project-profile-target-check: accept Validate declared profiles and