bilities, silently weakens safety or lacks a required registry grant. Emit Policy/capability diff, selected graph or refusal and PKG5002/PKG5005. Dependencies: PKG5, PKG6, PKG8, PKG9. Criterion behavior/pkg5/deterministic-dependency-solver: accept Canonicalize and record roots/constraints/profiles/targets/registries/priorities/lock/metadata/policies/features/ABI; use specified tie-breaks and lock selected direct/transitive versions/features/variants with full trust/safety/license metadata. Reject The same canonical input produces different choices, transitive releases remain unlocked or unrecorded default features introduce effects. Emit Resolution report, complete lock/diff, conflict/capability/variant/provenance/offline summaries and PKG5004/PKG5007/PKG5008. Dependencies: PKG1, PKG5, PKG11. Criterion behavior/pkg5/minimal-conflict-explanation: accept Explain unsatisfied version/feature constraints using the minimal known conflicting set and relevant dependency chain. Reject A conflict report omits sufficient constraint evidence to act on or claims an unproved globally minimal explanation. Emit Conflict report with requested ranges, selected version when any, chain/profile/target/policy and PKG5001/PKG5008. Dependencies: PKG5. Criterion behavior/pkg5/offline-locked-resolution: accept Resolve the complete locked/local population offline with no network access. Reject An incomplete lock is silently repaired through a hidden network read. Emit Resolution graph or PKG5004 and offline-resolution evidence. Dependencies: PKG5, PKG7. Criterion behavior/pkg5/private-latent-resolution: accept Select private/latent dependencies only under an explicit matching registry read/visibility and state policy grant. Reject Private reads occur without a grant or a latent name satisfies ordinary dependency constraints. Emit Registry/source selection and access decision; PKG5005. Dependencies: PKG5, PKG9. Criterion behavior/pkg5/target-variant-selection: accept Select and lock features/artifact variants for every profile/target/ABI pair and record their applicability. Reject A required target lacks a variant or a host/default variant is silently substituted. Emit Per-target variant table, lock/diff and PKG5003. Dependencies: PKG5, PKG11. Allocation interface/safety/safe14/manifest-gate (Open). Role: build owning producer or consuming-boundary checker. Input: package resolution/build/update input with manifests, locks, dependencies and generated outputs. Required positive predicate: Declare package runtime/build/unsafe/native/plugin/generated/denied authority in safety metadata and fail conflicting imports during resolution before compiling dependents. Positive output witness: Validated safety manifest and resolution-time policy gate before dependent compilation. Concrete negative case: An import whose runtime/build/unsafe/native/plugin/generated/denied manifest conflicts with policy reaches dependent compilation. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/bind-compiler-decisions-to-runtimebuild-enforcement-hooks supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-safe-code-classification-and-taintunsafe-boundaries supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred. Allocation interface/safety/safe14/native-declarations (Open). Role: build owning producer or consuming-boundary checker. Input: package resolution/build/update input with manifests, locks, dependencies and generated outputs. Required positive predicate: Reject undeclared native dependencies in safe builds and require source/digest, version/ABI/targets/link/license/wrapper/authority/advisory metadata. Positive output witness: Native dependency declarations and safe-build unsupported/undeclared dependency refusal. Concrete negative case: A native dependency lacks pinned source/digest/version/ABI/targets/link/license/wrapper/authority metadata. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/bind-compiler-decisions-to-runtimebuild-enforcement-hooks supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-safe-code-classification-and-taintunsafe-boundaries supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred. Allocation interface/safety/safe14/transitive-authority (Open). Role: build owning producer or consuming-boundary checker. Input: package resolution/build/update input with manifests, locks, dependencies and generated outputs. Required positive predicate: Require root/deployment approval for dependency authority, compute transitive capabilities/effects/unsafe/native/plugins/model/tools/secrets/generated changes and present a safety diff on every authority-changing update. Positive output witness: Transitive authority closure/change diff and root/deployment approval decision. Concrete negative case: An update silently expands dependency capabilities, build effects, unsafe/native/plugin/model/tool/secret authority without root approval and safety diff. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/bind-compiler-decisions-to-runtimebuild-enforcement-hooks supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-safe-code-classification-and-taintunsafe-boundaries supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred. Allocation interface/safety/safe14/unsafe-policy (Open). Role: build owning producer or consuming-boundary checker. Input: package resolution/build/update input with manifests, locks, dependencies and generated outputs. Required positive predicate: Report dependency unsafe inventory, affected profiles, wrappers, reviews, certificates and unsafe dependencies so caller policy can gate unknown/expired/unwrapped/forbidden unsafe code. Positive output witness: Dependency unsafe inventory/families/profiles/reviews/wrappers/certificates and caller-policy verdict. Concrete negative case: A package with unknown/expired unsafe islands or missing safe wrappers is admitted under a forbidding caller policy. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/bind-compiler-decisions-to-runtimebuild-enforcement-hooks supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-safe-code-classification-and-taintunsafe-boundaries supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred."},
