     "- [ ] `build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/execute-typed-graph-under-declared-build-effects` Execute typed graph under declared build effects\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Build architecture](../../docs/phase-12-build-package-and-artifact-system/166-pkg2-build-system-architecture.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Clean build node receipts and undeclared environment/network/shell rejection. SAFE14 also denies undeclared postinstall, model/tool, compiler IR and unproven native generation/registry authority; permitted effects carry provider, scope, grant and trace, and hermetic release effects are replayable or have pinned outputs. Negative fixtures prove denial occurs before the external effect. Criterion `integration/build-input-capture`: Capture all declared external, session, configuration and script inputs affecting build outputs in reproducibility artifacts, or reject/mark nonhermetic behavior according to build policy. Accepted fixture: Capture declared external/session/configuration/script/environment/network/file inputs affecting build outputs with source and generator provenance. Negative fixture: Reject unrecorded nonhermetic influence or explicitly mark it according to the declared reproducibility policy; never silently certify hermeticity. Required evidence: build-input manifest and clean/replayed input-drift fixture; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime, schema outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed. Source obligation `language/compiletime/preserve-phase-artifacts`: Schedule compile-time stages in the declared semantic order and prevent later stages or memoization from mutating earlier artifacts or losing original source/generated provenance. Accept: Schedule reading, namespace loading, expansion, name/type/effect analysis, profile/capability validation, constant evaluation, extension execution, revalidated typed-core lowering and target preparation in L12 order. Later stages may inspect immutable prior artifacts; normalization and memoization retain original spans and generated-origin chains. Reject: Reject an out-of-order dependency, unauthorized extension/target preparation, mutation of a prior artifact or loss of original/generated diagnostic provenance. Required outputs: Ordered compile-time event graph, immutable before/after artifact digests, authorization decisions and source/generated-origin diagnostic fixtures. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from expand/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/expand5-integrate-generated-programs, types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types4-preserve-and-invalidate-facts, effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Criterion behavior/pkg2/declared-build-effects: accept Execute graph nodes only with declared allowed effects and actual grants; deny network after dependency resolution except an explicitly allowed step. Reject A step or plugin hides shell/network/environment effects, expands compiled-code authority or performs the operation after denial. Emit Node effect/grant decisions and PKG2001/PKG2007/PKG2008 before the external effect. Dependencies: L6, L15, PKG2, PKG6. Criterion behavior/pkg2/generated-build-inputs: accept Record generator identity, inputs, output provenance edge and re-enter generated source through the normal reader/checkers. Reject Generated source lacks a provenance edge or bypasses ordinary source legality checks. Emit Generated-source provenance edges, normal-pipeline results and PKG2003. Dependencies: C1, PKG2, PKG10. Criterion behavior/pkg2/graph-failure-location: accept A failed graph execution identifies the actual failing node and input edge with input/output identity and active policy. Reject A node/edge failure is hidden behind an unrelated later generic error. Emit Structured build diagnostic with node id, input hash, output id, effect, key field, profile, target and policy. Dependencies: PKG2, C15. Criterion behavior/pkg2/typed-build-graph: accept Construct typed graph nodes from project/lock inputs with declared inputs/outputs/effects/cache keys/tool/environment facts and artifact ids; admit only explicitly marked bootstrap fixed-point cycles. Reject A node omits a declared contract or an ordinary dependency cycle is treated as an approved compiler-bootstrap cycle. Emit Graph manifest, dependency edges, per-node execution and cache records; PKG2004 for an unapproved cycle. Dependencies: PKG1, PKG2, C1. Allocation interface/safety/safe14/build-authority (Open). Role: build owning producer or consuming-boundary checker. Input: package resolution/build/update input with manifests, locks, dependencies and generated outputs. Required positive predicate: Deny hidden build/postinstall/network/shell/environment/model/tool/IR/native/registry activity by default; permitted effects require grants/providers/scopes/traces and hermetic releases require replayable effects or pinned outputs. Positive output witness: Build provider/scope/grant/trace and replay/pinned-output decision before the external effect. Concrete negative case: A package performs undeclared postinstall/network/shell/environment/model/tool/IR/native/registry work or an unreplayable hermetic effect. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/bind-compiler-decisions-to-runtimebuild-enforcement-hooks supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-safe-code-classification-and-taintunsafe-boundaries supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred."},
