     "- [ ] `build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-dependency-aware-caching-and-invalidation` Implement dependency-aware caching and invalidation\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Pass cache](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/pass_cache.clj)\n\nClosing evidence: Reuse on equal inputs; rebuild on source, compiler, grant, policy or target changes Source compiler/c16/cache-revalidation: Reuse stage-specific entries only after producing-pass/schema/version/facts/policy/dependency/diagnostic validation, retaining provenance and invalidation records. Concrete acceptance: Change producer pass version, schema, preserved facts, profile/target, policy, dependency or diagnostic schema separately; reject stale reuse and record the actual affected revalidation/recomputation, keeping prior provenance. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source compiler/c16/proof-reuse: Reuse proofs/certificates only when complete claim/input/assumption/context/invalidation conditions match; require a mapping when node identity changes but semantics survive. Concrete acceptance: Change each claim/input/assumption/profile/target/compiler/provider/package/invalidation premise, and change a node ID without a proof mapping; reject reuse or reprove, retaining residual checks until evidence is valid. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source compiler/c16/recorded-rebuild: Reproduce hermetic/release artifacts from recorded inputs and replay rather than trusting stale or incomplete caches. Concrete acceptance: Remove or alter a recorded build input or effect replay record; the hermetic/release rebuild must refuse the claim or expose output drift rather than passing from a stale cache. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source compiler/c16/semantic-cache-key: Key each reusable stage artifact over all meaning/legality/proof/diagnostic/output inputs with producer-owned required fields; reject incomplete or timestamp-only identity. Concrete acceptance: Omit each producer-required semantic/legality/proof/diagnostic/output input, or provide only a timestamp; reject C16-KEY and demonstrate that each changed relevant field prevents a false cache hit. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Source compiler/c16/speculation-publication-gate: Mark partial interactive reuse speculative and withhold release publication until full revalidation succeeds. Concrete acceptance: Attempt publication from a partially revalidated interactive cache; require C16-SPECULATIVE and no release artifact until complete revalidation succeeds. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Criterion behavior/pkg2/dependency-aware-cache: accept Reuse equal source, lockfile, compiler, profile, target, policy and relevant environment inputs with a matching cache key. Reject Changing any consumed source, lock, compiler, profile, target, safety policy, capability grant or relevant environment input still reuses the cached artifact. Emit Input hashes and reused/rebuilt node/cache-decision log with changed key field and PKG2002. Dependencies: PKG2, PKG7, C16. Decision allocation interface/compiler/c16/dependency-invalidation (Open). Role: build cache/invalidation maintainer. Invalidate downstream artifacts on every specified source/macro/namespace/type/effect/profile/capability/safety/proof/provider/target/backend/package/policy/facet/diagnostic change; record exact affected revalidation stages. Refusals and conditional cases: Change source, reader option/extension, macro/dependency, grant/replay, namespace import/export/alias, package version, type/provider, effect/capability registry, profile, safety/proof/trust, pass contract, target/backend, runtime/provider, facet or diagnostic schema; reject stale reuse and record each affected downstream revalidation stage. Required outputs: Field-sensitive dependency graph, complete change-class invalidation trace and clean-versus-revalidated artifact/diagnostic comparison. Consume actual dependency interface outputs: resolve/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/resolve4-publish-stable-indexes, pipeline; whole-component completion is not a prerequisite. Retain exact source/compiler/pass/profile/target and checker/provider identities, actual positive products and refused-case diagnostics. Implementation acceptance remains unassessed."},
