     "- [ ] `build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/close-reproducibility-and-target-matrix` Close reproducibility and target matrix\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Reproducibility contract](../../docs/phase-12-build-package-and-artifact-system/171-pkg7-reproducible-build-specification.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Repeated locked builds with matching identities and explicit failing-target diagnostics Foundation requirement gravity/artifact-graph-reproducibility: Rebuild the declared artifact graph from recorded source/compiler/pass/policy/provider/target and dependency identities; compare canonical graph edges and outputs under an explicit accepted-delta policy. Refusals: Reject omitted inputs or edges, substituted provider/compiler identities and unexplained output drift; preserve the failed comparison and any policy-reviewed exception. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products; runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-explicit-family-selection-and-no-runtime-rejection - Selected runtime/provider service contracts and actual link/load/service-use evidence. Source obligation `language/compiletime/reproduce-hermetic-core`: Reproduce byte-identical typed core from declared semantic inputs in required hermetic release/conformance/publication/safety-critical modes, rejecting undeclared ambient inputs. Accept: In release, conformance, reproducible publication and safety-critical modes, repeat the same source/compiler/lock/target/grants/declared inputs and require byte-identical typed core. Declare environment key/value policy, pin or replay network/shell/model/tool/package inputs, record clock/random values or deterministic seeds, use declared target manifests and hash generated inputs. Native-object metadata differences require a marked nonsemantic field and target conformance acceptance. Reject: Reject undeclared filesystem/environment input, unrecorded nondeterminism, ambient target probing, typed-core drift or an unreviewed native-object exception; report L12-HERMETIC-INPUT or L12-NONDETERMINISM as applicable. Required outputs: Hermetic input/replay manifest, paired typed-core byte comparison, generated-input hashes, exception record when applicable and accepted/rejected diagnostics. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from expand/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/expand5-integrate-generated-programs, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime, build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/execute-typed-graph-under-declared-build-effects; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Criterion behavior/pkg11/explicit-target-fallback: accept Use a fallback target/runtime only when explicitly declared and compatible with project/profile/policy. Reject A failed target silently falls back to a different target or runtime. Emit Visible fallback selection in target/artifact records and PKG11007. Dependencies: PKG11, P13. Criterion behavior/pkg11/host-independent-cross-compile: accept Resolve and compile target profile/backend/runtime/ABI contracts independently of implicit host ABI, services and paths. Reject A cross build inherits host ABI/paths/default target assumptions. Emit Target-specific build/artifact identity and host-leakage rejection with PKG11002. Dependencies: PKG11, B1, R1. Criterion behavior/pkg11/per-target-evidence: accept Attach required conformance and support-level evidence separately to each target and expose every failing profile/target pair. Reject Default-target success hides a required target failure or a release claims support without its per-target conformance. Emit Per-target test/conformance reports, support table and PKG11006. Dependencies: PKG11, TEST3, TEST4, TEST6. Criterion behavior/pkg11/target-compatibility-admission: accept Validate profile/backend legality, dependency variants and capability availability for every concrete target before lowering. Reject A pair is unsupported, contradicts project profiles, lacks a dependency variant or assumes capabilities legal on another target. Emit Checked matrix, per-target graph/capability decision and PKG11001/PKG11003/PKG11004/PKG11008. Dependencies: PKG11, PKG5, P13, B1. Criterion behavior/pkg11/target-matrix-artifact: accept Normalize grouped declarations into concrete profile/backend/triple/ABI/calling-convention/runtime/features/dependency/capability/artifact/test/support entries and emit each target's manifests and support level. Reject Required target/ABI identity is missing, a matrix contradicts the project or a supported claim lacks its target-specific record. Emit Normalized matrix, dependency graph, capability summary, artifact/test/conformance manifests and supported/experimental/internal/build-only/unsupported table; PKG11005/PKG11008. Dependencies: PKG1, PKG11, R1, B1. Criterion behavior/pkg7/canonical-rebuild-comparison: accept Compare canonical manifests and actual content hashes for two locked builds under the same recipe, explaining only declared differences. Reject Verification compares filenames alone or ignores a changed canonical content/manifest identity. Emit Expected/actual digest lists and rebuild verification report; PKG7007. Dependencies: PKG3, PKG7. Criterion behavior/pkg7/deterministic-build-environment: accept Control source/project/lock/compiler/toolchain/graph/profile/target/environment/locale/timezone/order/timestamps/seeds/network/generated/blob/FFI inputs; normalize time/order/paths and seed or record randomness. Reject A reproducible build uses unlocked dependencies, unrecorded external reads/randomness, leaked host paths or generated source without generator/input hashes. Emit Controlled environment and input/output manifests, build recipe, exception list and PKG7002-PKG7006; changed compiler invalidates cache. Dependencies: PKG7, PKG2, PKG10. Criterion behavior/pkg7/nonreproducible-claim-boundary: accept Mark uncontrolled-input artifacts nonreproducible and list their exceptions explicitly. Reject A nonreproducible artifact satisfies a reproducible release/signing gate or a reproducibility claim lacks its recipe. Emit Nonreproducibility exception and release decision; PKG7001/PKG7008. Dependencies: PKG7, PKG12. Criterion behavior/pkg7/recorded-build-recipe: accept Emit a schema-valid release build recipe binding package/version, source/project/lock/compiler/toolchain, graph/task settings, concrete profile/target matrix, controlled environment/locale/timezone/traversal/timestamps/seeds/network, generator/input hashes, blobs/FFI inputs, expected artifact identities, output hashes and verification command or machine-readable equivalent. Rebuild twice under that exact recipe and compare canonical manifests and actual content hashes. For standard-library packages retain source commit, build graph, compiler, package lock, tests and policy-required signatures in the provenance record. Reject Reject a claimed reproducible release with no recipe, omitted or altered consumed inputs/outputs, unlocked dependencies, unrecorded network/randomness, host path leakage, missing generator hashes, filename-only comparison or unexplained hash drift; mark uncontrolled inputs nonreproducible and deny reproducible signing/release claims when policy requires reproducibility. Standard-library provenance and artifact identity must agree; neither API inventory nor a supplied success label proves a rebuild. Emit Versioned build-recipe artifact, controlled-environment manifest, input/output digest lists, actual repeat-build canonical comparison, exception list and PKG7001-PKG7008 diagnostics with recipe/input/artifact/target/environment context; standard-library source/build/lock/test/signature provenance links. Dependencies: PKG1/PKG2 project, lock and typed graph producers, PKG3 canonical manifests, PKG5 complete dependency lock, PKG10/PKG12 provenance/signing evidence, stdlib/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/integrate-platform-modules-and-close-release-manifests module/package manifests, BOOT6 trust evidence remains separate."},
