     "- [ ] `cli/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/connect-checkruncompilebuildtestpackageverify-to-real-services` Connect check/run/compile/build/test/package/verify to real services\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Compile dispatcher](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/cli/compile_command.clj)\n\nClosing evidence: Executed success/failure fixtures and artifact paths at public command boundary T1 acceptance: actual command execution records and artifact paths/manifest hashes retain declared grants/denials. Reject ungranted effects, silent unsafe/AI/network/shell/secrets/publish operations, hidden network, output-directory escape without grant and missing release artifact verification. Foundation requirement gravity/hosted-hello-execution: Compile the D2 hosted hello source through actual Reader, Syntax, macro expansion and hosted execution, preserving stage/source identities and recording the declared stdout effect and granted authority with the produced output. Refusals: Reject malformed source and the same program without stdout authority; a static hello manifest, host-language print or supplied output string cannot establish execution. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products; runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-explicit-family-selection-and-no-runtime-rejection - Selected runtime/provider service contracts and actual link/load/service-use evidence. Release extension release/public-check-command: Through the public gravity executable, check declared hello, core and nontrivial applications for both .qst and .gravity. Retain expected check results/artifacts, exact source path/extension, executable/compiler identity and normalized command stdout/stderr. Internal calls or relabelled extensions are not public command evidence. Reject missing parity with P18T04001 and invalid inputs with owning diagnostics. Release extension release/public-run-command: Run each declared hello/core/nontrivial application through public gravity under its declared runtime/grants for both canonical extensions; compare actual output/exit with fixture expectations. Preserve supplied source path/kind and normalized transcripts. Reject missing public execution, incorrect output or hidden delegated runtime failure; manifest presence and internal evaluator results do not establish public run. Release extension release/public-compile-output-command: Execute gravity compile for declared hello/core/nontrivial applications in both canonical extensions, including requested -o locations. Retain actual executable outputs/hashes, sidecars/provenance, compiler identity and original source paths/extensions. Reject missing/substituted executable, ignored output location, invalid target, provenance mismatch and command parity failure; supplied candidate records alone are not compilation. Release extension release/generated-application-execution: Invoke the exact artifacts emitted by public compile, including the declared core-app executable, and compare hello/core/nontrivial outputs/exits under declared runtime or no-runtime boundaries. Bind execution to emitted hashes and original provenance for both extensions. Reject missing, substituted, non-executable or behaviorally wrong outputs; successful compilation cannot replace generated-application execution. Release extension release/public-rejection-diagnostics: Exercise parser, semantic/arity, capability, package and release invalid applications through the same public executable. Preserve owning stable code, applicable span/manifest/profile/source context, non-success exit and normalized stdout/stderr; prove paired extension/path rejection parity. Include applicable L1-DELIMITER, L2-FUNCTION-ARITY, P4-HOST-CAPABILITY, PKG10001 and B13-RELEASE cases. Reject swallowed failure, generic substituted categories and invalid success. Release extension release/public-subset-test-bridge: Exercise gravity test's bootstrap-hosted current-public-subset bridge through accepted check/run/compile/generated-execution and rejected stable-diagnostic cases, retaining source paths and both canonical extensions. Proof names actual subset and hosting. Reject test --full and full-language/self-hosted-runner overclaims with P18T04006. Retain this bounded surface separately from final self-hosted full-language conformance. Release extension release/public-incomplete-selfhost-verifier: While final seed retirement or release is incomplete, public gravity self-host verify writes an honest incomplete proof with active compiler source path/extension and seed facts, then fails closed with P18T04007. Invalid self-host invocation rejects with P18T04008. Exercise both through the public boundary. Incomplete proof production or hosted command availability cannot establish final successful self-host verification. Tooling decision interface/behavior/t1/explicit-command-context: Route declared CLI command families to actual component services under explicit project/profile/target/policy context without silently granting privileged effects. Required source-defined acceptance predicates (subject to their stated conditions): declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/1012-1031: - `gravity audit`; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/1031-1051: - `gravity verify`; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/1051-1075: - `gravity inspect-ir`; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/1075-1096: - `gravity profile`; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/1096-1112: - `gravity ai`; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/1313-1422: - Commands MUST accept explicit project, profile, target, package, and output format options where relevant. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/1754-1821: - Commands that request capabilities MUST show grants and denials. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/1821-1914: - Unsafe, AI, network, shell, secrets, and package-publish operations MUST not run silently. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/2118-2139: - `0` means success. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/2188-2217: - `2` means CLI usage error. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/2217-2271: - `3` means dependency or registry resolution failed. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/2328-2366: - `5` means runtime execution failed. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/2366-2425: - `6` means required authority or human-review is missing. ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t1/2832-2847: The CLI emits: ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t1/2941-2970: - command execution records; ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t1/2970-3000: - trace files when requested; ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t1/3000-3029: - shell-completion metadata; ; negative-acceptance facet/ai-build-tools/t1/3402-3495: - Reject commands that infer profile or target when the project requires explicit selection. ; negative-acceptance facet/ai-build-tools/t1/3495-3563: - Reject operations requiring capabilities without declared grants. ; negative-acceptance facet/ai-build-tools/t1/3563-3625: - Reject release commands with missing artifact verification. ; negative-acceptance facet/ai-build-tools/t1/3720-3810: - Reject output paths outside allowed build/output directories unless explicitly granted. ; negative-acceptance facet/ai-build-tools/t1/3810-3863: - Reject commands that would expose secrets in logs. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t1/3944-3989: - `T1001` reports missing profile or target. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t1/4034-4070: - `T1003` reports authority denial. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t1/4165-4206: - `T1006` reports invalid command usage. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t1/4248-4289: - `T1008` reports hidden network access. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t1/4448-4528: - Diagnostics include profile, target, source span or manifest path when known. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t1/4584-4654: - Artifact-producing commands print and emit artifact manifest paths. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t1/4654-4744: - CI can run `check`, `test`, `build`, `audit`, and `verify` without parsing human prose. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/826-845: - `gravity check`; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/845-864: - `gravity build`; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/864-882: - `gravity test`; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/882-899: - `gravity run`; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/899-917: - `gravity repl`; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/917-934: - `gravity fmt`; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/934-952: - `gravity lint`; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/952-969: - `gravity doc`; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/969-990: - `gravity package`; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/990-1012: - `gravity registry`; Produce actual service evidence and owning rejection diagnostics for the applicable positive/negative cases; links, record flags and another service's success do not establish this behavior. Implementation remains Open."},
