     "- [ ] `cli/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/connect-replformatlintdocinspectprofileauditairegistryexplain-services` Connect REPL/format/lint/doc/inspect/profile/audit/AI/registry/explain services\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Tooling contracts](../../docs/phase-13-tooling-and-developer-experience/README.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Each declared command has a genuine service result and negative fixture; no metadata-only success T1 acceptance: gravity explain resolves known diagnostic codes and artifact ids to actionable source/policy context. Each invoked T2-T13 service keeps its own semantic owner and positive/negative service evidence. Tooling decision interface/behavior/t1/explain-command-decision: Explain a command's actual diagnostic, policy and artifact decision using the source component's facts. Required source-defined acceptance predicates (subject to their stated conditions): declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/1112-1133: - `gravity explain`. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/1914-2011: - `gravity explain` MUST resolve diagnostic codes and artifact ids to source and policy context. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/2139-2188: - `1` means diagnostics failed policy or checks. ; negative-acceptance facet/ai-build-tools/t1/3863-3927: - Reject hidden network access outside package or build policy. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t1/4744-4819: - `gravity explain` resolves known diagnostic codes to actionable context. Produce actual service evidence and owning rejection diagnostics for the applicable positive/negative cases; links, record flags and another service's success do not establish this behavior. Implementation remains Open."},
