     "- [ ] `cli/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/normalize-json-text-exit-codes-and-redaction` Normalize JSON, text, exit codes and redaction\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Diagnostic presentation](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/cli/diagnostic_presentation.clj)\n\nClosing evidence: Golden success/error outputs including source, target, grants and redacted secrets T1 acceptance: golden JSON success/failure per family; exits 0 success, 1 policy/check, 2 usage, 3 dependency/registry, 4 build/artifact, 5 runtime, 6 missing authority/review. Reports include code/severity/source-span-or-manifest/profile/target/remediation when available, artifact paths/hashes and redacted text/JSON; CI check/test/build/audit/verify consume JSON. Reject unavailable requested JSON and unstable plugin output. Tooling decision interface/behavior/t1/cli-redaction: Keep secrets and protected payloads out of CLI output, logs and diagnostic contexts. Required source-defined acceptance predicates (subject to their stated conditions): declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/2011-2045: - CLI output MUST redact secrets. ; negative-acceptance facet/ai-build-tools/t1/3810-3863: - Reject commands that would expose secrets in logs. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t1/4119-4165: - `T1005` reports secret redaction violation. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t1/4528-4584: - Secret values are redacted from text and JSON output. Produce actual service evidence and owning rejection diagnostics for the applicable positive/negative cases; links, record flags and another service's success do not establish this behavior. Implementation remains Open. Tooling decision interface/behavior/t1/stable-command-results: Return the specified stable exit classes and structured JSON diagnostic/artifact path/hash results for success and each failure category; the golden CLI fixtures are acceptance facets of these results, not service implementation credit. Required source-defined acceptance predicates (subject to their stated conditions): declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/1422-1464: - Commands MUST return stable exit codes. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/1464-1557: - Commands MUST support JSON output for automation when they produce diagnostics or reports. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/1557-1679: - Diagnostics MUST include code, severity, source span or manifest path, profile, target, and remediation when available. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/1679-1754: - Build and package commands MUST emit artifact paths and manifest hashes. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/2045-2102: - CLI behavior MUST be testable through golden fixtures. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/2139-2188: - `1` means diagnostics failed policy or checks. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t1/2271-2328: - `4` means build graph or artifact verification failed. ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t1/2848-2869: - human text output; ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t1/2869-2896: - structured JSON reports; ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t1/2896-2918: - diagnostic streams; ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t1/2918-2941: - artifact path lists; ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t1/3029-3062: - golden output fixture schemas. ; negative-acceptance facet/ai-build-tools/t1/3563-3625: - Reject release commands with missing artifact verification. ; negative-acceptance facet/ai-build-tools/t1/3625-3720: - Reject scripts relying on unstable human output when JSON mode is requested but unavailable. ; negative-acceptance facet/ai-build-tools/t1/3720-3810: - Reject output paths outside allowed build/output directories unless explicitly granted. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t1/3989-4034: - `T1002` reports unsupported output format. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t1/4070-4119: - `T1004` reports artifact verification failure. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t1/4206-4248: - `T1007` reports unstable plugin output. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t1/4315-4407: - Each command family has at least one golden JSON success fixture and one failure fixture. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t1/4407-4448: - Exit codes match the documented table. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t1/4448-4528: - Diagnostics include profile, target, source span or manifest path when known. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t1/4528-4584: - Secret values are redacted from text and JSON output. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t1/4584-4654: - Artifact-producing commands print and emit artifact manifest paths. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t1/4744-4819: - `gravity explain` resolves known diagnostic codes to actionable context. Produce actual service evidence and owning rejection diagnostics for the applicable positive/negative cases; links, record flags and another service's success do not establish this behavior. Implementation remains Open."},
