erflow/precision or rounding/NaN-policy loss, ambiguous branch/unit conversion and symbolic equality without valid evidence. Keep independent source conflicts on particular conversion modes open rather than choosing an undocumented policy. Required outputs: Numeric-kind lattice, conversion-rule table, machine-readable support matrix/mode/provider records, EFIR annotations and conformance cases for every supported conversion/family; MATH1-FAMILY/CONVERSION/NARROW/PRECISION/ROUNDING/BRANCH/ALLOCATION/EQUALITY/PROFILE diagnostics with span/family/mode/profile/target/provider/proof. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types2-check-declared-abstractions, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower1-validate-lowering-inputs interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping math/numeric-profile-eligibility; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred.\n\nMath source-specific implementation criteria (proposed adoption, all Open).\nThese stable criterion IDs refine the existing literal `math` task; they do not add\nproject tasks or mark any implementation accepted. Each dependency names an input\ninterface and can be satisfied by its exact available artifact, not completion of\nthe whole component. Each declared supported case needs actual positive and negative\nexecution evidence before closure; unavailable combinations remain explicit.\n\nCurrent AGENTS accounting-removal policy governs historical fuel/depth/node/time/candidate-count passages: no project work allowance or otherwise-valid-input quota is an admission requirement. Preserve deterministic choices, semantic legality, complete proof/partition/trace evidence and truthful unresolved outcomes. Declared runtime performance obj