     "- [ ] `evolution/library-admission` Admit standard modules and exports with full release evidence\n\nStatus: Open\n\nSource requirement: `governance/library-admission`\n\nRequired outputs: Module ownership/stability/profile manifests and export inventories API/profile/safety/security/compatibility/conformance/release review record tied to each admitted revision\n\nClosing evidence: Inventory module owner, stability, supported profiles, artifact schema and conformance suite; each export declares type/effect/capability/allocation/error/diagnostic/profile/stability metadata. Positive and negative fixtures cover each supported/rejected profile, capability boundary and documentation example; unsafe wrappers carry GOV9 audits and all preconditions. Host delegation carries provider/target records; GOV2 breaking-change analysis, STD20/GOV8 stabilization and reproducible signed provenance/SBOM accompany release. Actual complete accepted artifact and consumer result for the named source contract, with input/source/policy/tool identity. Historical stage0 records or a passing schema alone do not implement these outcomes.\n\nRequired rejection evidence: Reject missing module owner/stability, incomplete export metadata, unsupported profiles, unaudited wrappers, missing capability fixtures and hidden providers. Reject stabilization without conformance/compatibility history or package release without provenance/signature/SBOM. Malformed/missing/stale/wrong-scope records and each named source rejection produce the original GOV diagnostics at the actual consuming boundary.\n\nDependencies: STD1-STD20 actual library export fixtures; GOV2 compatibility and GOV8 stabilization; GOV4 security and GOV9 unsafe review; PKG release provenance/signatures/SBOM. Dependencies are required artifacts/conditional consumers, not a claim their producer tasks are implemented or a cyclic all-tasks-complete gate.\n\nExact source criteria: facet/bootstrap-governance/ced143c1ce4b6d478f6b5ff9, facet/b