     "- [ ] `evolution/namespace-decision` Govern reservation, transfer and abandoned namespace takeover\n\nStatus: Open\n\nSource requirement: `governance/namespace-decision`\n\nRequired outputs: Owned namespace reservation/transfer/takeover decision and owner-verification audit artifact\n\nClosing evidence: Apply declared namespace and reserved-name policy, verify the actual owner for transfer, and retain reason/decision/history for reservation, dispute or abandoned-package takeover. Publish audit references usable by registries/package policy without exposing private namespace information or treating identity lookup as authorization. Actual complete accepted artifact and consumer result for the named source contract, with input/source/policy/tool identity. Historical stage0 records or a passing schema alone do not implement these outcomes.\n\nRequired rejection evidence: Reject transfer without verified ownership and audit record, reserved-name abuse, standard-library impersonation and unmitigated dependency-confusion risk. Do not infer an automatic takeover interval or let Build/Auth mechanics adjudicate governance policy. Malformed/missing/stale/wrong-scope records and each named source rejection produce the original GOV diagnostics at the actual consuming boundary.\n\nDependencies: GOV10 registry identity/ownership policy; PKG9 namespace/private-registry facts; GOV4 supply-chain review when relevant. Dependencies are required artifacts/conditional consumers, not a claim their producer tasks are implemented or a cyclic all-tasks-complete gate.\n\nExact source criteria: facet/bootstrap-governance/5278996755efd7c635deddf8, facet/bootstrap-governance/edcfd7d4957751f76b5655b8, facet/bootstrap-governance/9b8c71fd62a70ea16d27b359, facet/bootstrap-governance/69c0d07980e8f00b73c8ec9e, facet/bootstrap-governance/725b6496a1c3494ae47c66b8, facet/bootstrap-governance/961b6f80528a574c47900129, facet/bootstrap-governance/0ff8c58df9a54b696418b4cd, facet/bootstrap-governance/0