     "- [ ] `evolution/registry-yank` Publish yank decisions with preserved historical resolution\n\nStatus: Open\n\nSource requirement: `governance/registry-yank`\n\nRequired outputs: Yank action with reason/replacement, release/version identity and dependency-resolution behavior Retained lock/content identity and emergency-exception provenance\n\nClosing evidence: A yank prevents policy-forbidden new selection while retaining existing reproducible locks and historical artifacts. Record reason, replacement guidance and exact resolution behavior; accountable security governance controls emergency exceptions, while package/registry consumers enforce them. Actual complete accepted artifact and consumer result for the named source contract, with input/source/policy/tool identity. Historical stage0 records or a passing schema alone do not implement these outcomes.\n\nRequired rejection evidence: Reject missing reason/replacement/resolution metadata, erasure or silent mutation of old lock/content identity and unrecorded emergency overrides. A resolver refusal alone does not publish a yank action or produce its governance record. Malformed/missing/stale/wrong-scope records and each named source rejection produce the original GOV diagnostics at the actual consuming boundary.\n\nDependencies: GOV10 yank/advisory policy; GOV2 compatibility and GOV4 emergency disposition; PKG4/PKG9 history retention and PKG5 selection/install enforcement. Dependencies are required artifacts/conditional consumers, not a claim their producer tasks are implemented or a cyclic all-tasks-complete gate.\n\nExact source criteria: facet/bootstrap-governance/53c56836f5fa7ca7c04c67fb, facet/bootstrap-governance/69f29b4973b533f0a59e8441."},
