     "- [ ] `evolution/rfc-review` Produce the formal RFC payload and traceable review dossier\n\nStatus: Open\n\nSource requirement: `governance/rfc-review`\n\nRequired outputs: RFC id/owner/status/scope/review owners/affected documents and durable decision history Complete substantive proposal and specialist review dossier with implementation/conformance/release links\n\nClosing evidence: For nontrivial semantic changes supply motivation, design/examples, contracts, profile/target/type/effect/capability/memory/artifact/diagnostic impact, safety/security, alternatives, rollout/implementation, tests, migration and stabilization/removal criteria before final decision. Keep editorial ordinary-review exception; formal review states and accountable approval belong to the change-review task, distinct from this proposal producer and the changed feature implementation. Retain source-qualified split to governance/rfc-proposal-artifact and governance/change-review; complete rejected/withdrawn proposals remain inspectable. Accepted RFCs trace to implementation/conformance before release. Actual complete accepted artifact and consumer result for the named source contract, with input/source/policy/tool identity. Historical stage0 records or a passing schema alone do not implement these outcomes.\n\nRequired rejection evidence: Reject ownerless/unbounded RFCs, missing affected contracts/required sections/plans/history, unsupported safe-code changes and incompatible changes without GOV2 analysis. Reject security/unsafe/library/package/experimental/stabilization changes without applicable specialist records, unclear rollback/stabilization criteria and accepted RFCs lacking implementation/validation links. Malformed/missing/stale/wrong-scope records and each named source rejection produce the original GOV diagnostics at the actual consuming boundary.\n\nDependencies: Draft GOV1 change record, not completed change implementation; GOV2/GOV4/GOV3-STD20/GOV7/GOV8/GOV9/GOV10 applicable 