     "- [ ] `evolution/security-response` Produce incident response and a distinct actionable advisory\n\nStatus: Open\n\nSource requirement: `governance/security-response`\n\nRequired outputs: Embargo/disclosure/advisory/patch/backport/release response record Separate advisory payload with affected versions, severity, impact, patched versions, mitigations and provenance links\n\nClosing evidence: Preserve accountable disclosure timing, mitigation, patch/backport and release evidence; affected implementation owners supply actual patch evidence. Consume GOV2 compatibility/migration evidence for security breaks and explicit emergency exceptions; publish the complete advisory only under accountable disclosure policy. The historical GOV10 line110 facet is retained but routed to package-policy consumption by the accepted correction; it does not turn advisory consumption into incident review or payload production. Actual complete accepted artifact and consumer result for the named source contract, with input/source/policy/tool identity. Historical stage0 records or a passing schema alone do not implement these outcomes.\n\nRequired rejection evidence: Reject advisory payloads without affected/patched version/impact/mitigation/provenance data, silent embargo bypass and unsupported patch/backport/release claims. Reject security compatibility exceptions without GOV2/GOV4 evidence and lock-history breakage absent explicit emergency policy. Malformed/missing/stale/wrong-scope records and each named source rejection produce the original GOV diagnostics at the actual consuming boundary.\n\nDependencies: GOV4 security assessment and affected-component patch/backport evidence; GOV2 migration/compatibility exception; GOV10 registry/dependency advisory consumers. Dependencies are required artifacts/conditional consumers, not a claim their producer tasks are implemented or a cyclic all-tasks-complete gate.\n\nExact source criteria: facet/bootstrap-governance/2bf95166f918c67587e0b1e9,