     "- [ ] `evolution/security-review` Perform and record evidence-backed security review\n\nStatus: Open\n\nSource requirement: `governance/security-review`\n\nRequired outputs: Threat model, review scope, evidence, decision, residual risk and accepted mitigations Release-preserved security review references and applicable exception/advisory links\n\nClosing evidence: Before accepting authority/secret/taint/unsafe/FFI/plugin/host/AI/package changes, review actual trust boundaries and source evidence, not only metadata presence. Capability review includes least privilege/denial/redaction; secrets include lifetime/memory/serialization/retention; taint includes propagation/validation/sinks; unsafe/FFI/host/plugin changes include audit/boundary tests. AI review includes prompt-injection probes, tool authorization, ai/human-review and eval gates; supply-chain review includes identity/provenance/signature/SBOM/dependency confusion/malware. Accountable governance explicitly disposes high residual risk. Actual complete accepted artifact and consumer result for the named source contract, with input/source/policy/tool identity. Historical stage0 records or a passing schema alone do not implement these outcomes. Criterion governance/unsafe-audit-decision: Produce a distinct GOV9 specialist unsafe-audit decision for the exact island/source/owner/profile/target/wrapper revision, preserving the difference from a GOV4 security decision. Review every pre/postcondition, invariant, proof/runtime check and declared effect/capability, memory/alias/lifetime/initialization/concurrency/FFI/backend assumption using actual SAFE6 records, wrapper evidence, invalid-precondition negatives and applicable fuzz/sanitizer/model/formal/optimization-preservation results. Require GOV3/STD20 for standard-library islands and GOV4 for security impact. Emit scoped audit/verdict, evidence and stale/revalidation record, with package/release unsafe provenance. Revalidate after relevant compiler/optimizer/backend/target/profile/wrapper/dependency changes; deny stabilization/release with stale or missing audit, unenforced wrapper precondition, missing assumptions/specialist evidence, leaked unsafe public API or hidden provenance. Preserve GOV9001-GOV9008 and demonstrate valid review plus each applicable refusal. A generic security PASS or presence of an island record cannot substitute for this audit; ordinary development is not gated by it.\n\nRequired rejection evidence: Reject missing security review, authority expansion without evidence, secret leakage, unvalidated taint sinks, unaudited unsafe/host boundaries and AI tool expansion without policy/injection tests. Reject package changes without supply-chain analysis, security compatibility breaks without migration and unresolved high-risk release findings without explicit governance acceptance. Malformed/missing/stale/wrong-scope records and each named source rejection produce the original GOV diagnostics at the actual consuming boundary.\n\nDependencies: SAFE6/7/10/11/13/14/15/16 and A7/8/10/11 source-qualified evidence; Affected Auth/Legality/compiler/provider fixtures; GOV2 compatibility and package provenance/signatures/SBOM. Dependencies are required artifacts/conditional consumers, not a claim their producer tasks are implemented or a cyclic all-tasks-complete gate.\n\nExact source criteria: facet/bootstrap-governance/8b4a2b87f396f9d8606b1782, facet/bootstrap-governance/4af0872fde1e51a5376c1b02, facet/bootstrap-governance/f4178e95cce3c6b91ff5309b, facet/bootstrap-governance/1913c285d9856331f0adb40d, facet/bootstrap-governance/3a02ae5afb88b24109f03c97, facet/bootstrap-governance/2910be6fcb59d3f99bfa1f66, facet/bootstrap-governance/5d662210bd180d2f0e0dd883, facet/bootstrap-governance/1d9da04f273649afdfb2e39d, facet/bootstrap-governance/4e6ff6308560b9774cf01627, facet/bootstrap-governance/e3312a902bba0597d185ef1e, facet/bootstrap-governance/059828c8e517c8d6dcd200f6, facet/bootstrap-governance/c0b0f716a1c6ce2d2b17