     "- [ ] `evolution/stabilization-decision` Establish an exact stable contract and compatibility baseline\n\nStatus: Open\n\nSource requirement: `governance/stabilization-decision`\n\nRequired outputs: Stabilization record naming contract/surfaces, evidence and accountable decision Future compatibility baseline, package/tooling metadata and lifecycle release notes Owned deprecation/removal decision and record naming contract/export/profile surfaces, replacement or explicit no-replacement rationale, diagnostic id, warning/error/removal schedule, migration artifacts, retained-until-removal tests and release/package visibility; security emergency links to GOV4 and GOV2.\n\nClosing evidence: Require conformance history, negative fixtures, compatibility analysis, documentation and migration readiness for the exact surfaces; safety/security/library changes include applicable evidence and GOV4/GOV3/STD20 review. Close or update GOV7 experiment records; accepted RFC/module admission alone does not confer stability. Deprecation and removal retain replacement/rationale, diagnostic/schedule/migration and tests until removal under GOV8. Security emergency removals require both GOV4 and GOV2 records; release tooling lists stabilized/deprecated/removed contracts and source-qualified consumer outputs. Actual complete accepted artifact and consumer result for the named source contract, with input/source/policy/tool identity. Historical stage0 records or a passing schema alone do not implement these outcomes. Produce a governed deprecation record with replacement or explicit no-replacement rationale, structured diagnostic, warning/error/removal schedule and migration artifacts. Keep deprecated contracts supported and test-covered until the approved removal window; removal proceeds after that window or an explicit GOV4/GOV2 security emergency. Compiler diagnostics, docs, package warnings/rejection, migration tools or structured fix data and release notes consume the exact record. For standard-library exports preserve declared stability and compatibility dimensions; breaking source/behavior/effect/capability/diagnostic/artifact/profile/conformance changes carry impact analysis, migration, conformance updates and governance approval. Removing profile availability and tightening safety/capability/schema rules are explicitly classified by source/artifact impact; library release compatibility reports and signed provenance remain required inputs. Emit GOV8003-GOV8008 and STD20007 as applicable; historical or compatibility packages do not imply a removed API remains generally available.\n\nRequired rejection evidence: Reject evidence-free stabilization, missing compatibility surfaces, missing security/library review and experiments stabilized without GOV7 closure. Reject omitted lifecycle release metadata, missing migration readiness and premature removal without explicit emergency policy. Malformed/missing/stale/wrong-scope records and each named source rejection produce the original GOV diagnostics at the actual consuming boundary. Reject silent removal, missing replacement or rationale, diagnostic id or schedules, absent migration/fix data, premature removal without the explicit security exception, lost deprecated-contract tests, missing package metadata or lifecycle release notes and hidden profile/stability/compatibility changes. Reject standard-library breaking changes without impact/migration/conformance/governance evidence and emergency removal lacking both GOV4 and GOV2 records.\n\nDependencies: GOV2 compatibility baseline/report; GOV3/STD20 library and GOV4 safety/security review as applicable; GOV7 experiment closure and GOV8 lifecycle evidence; Affected component conformance history/negative fixtures/docs/migration metadata. Dependencies are required artifacts/conditional consumers, not a claim their producer tasks are implemented or a cyclic all-tasks-complete gate. GOV1 accountable change and GOV2 compatibility/migration evidence; GOV4 emergency authorization where applicable; GOV7 experiment closure when relevant; GOV3/STD20 library owner supplies export stability, compatibility reports and signed provenance; affected compiler/docs/package/migration/test/release owners produce actual consumer conformance and retained tests. The accountable lifecycle record does not substitute for their implementations.\n\nExact source criteria: facet/bootstrap-governance/d0e05b1ed2644e1fd2ce4b85, facet/bootstrap-governance/489b4263da8d23ddabd9e3ae, facet/bootstrap-governance/df842eeb4177a968623ac0a8, facet/bootstrap-governance/37be7f5bd2b4ae59e497d1dc, facet/bootstrap-governance/db8be9ed3c06f63372ff70b4, facet/bootstrap-governance/78c3423f45c1be476ad57dd9, facet/bootstrap-governance/2e9f5cf7506d3736da73112e, facet/bootstrap-governance/9cd815d35a827190fb4ea9c6, facet/bootstrap-governance/d2c7dd8882323ca560e37a99, facet/bootstrap-governance/d634d2f511cc86d514a6d273, facet/bootstrap-governance/07242484e572c5187957998e, facet/bootstrap-governance/a14a05f8a4b60af84326df49, facet/bootstrap-governance/ab2f0f63f41575436939bcdb, facet/bootstrap-governance/e77be9411c2e3a5ce64a216a, facet/bootstrap-governance/ae1a409d8759166b0124487b, facet/bootstrap-governance/6cf3e5c475d03002a6a0f926, facet/bootstrap-governance/71851eebba2ef5d5f0332d7d, facet/bootstrap-governance/9c7ba3bc06e4bbd463c47194, facet/bootstrap-governance/3f3bf717df0f53d9b7fa4cf7, facet/bootstrap-governance/214aa4b6095b637daf154a40, facet/bootstrap-governance/849233a58c888af074151884, facet/bootstrap-governance/48ce65ab7cf428db0d10af20, facet/bootstrap-governance/b7c9748e4bb4a4bae11ce067, facet/bootstrap-governance/9d26093d9d0953d512e6227f."},
