     "- [ ] `evolution/target-support-admission` Admit and maintain target support tiers from actual evidence\n\nStatus: Open\n\nSource requirement: `governance/target-support-admission`\n\nRequired outputs: Target tier/owner/profile/unsupported-surface/backend/runtime record Tier promotion/maintenance/deprecation/removal decision with actual conformance and release evidence\n\nClosing evidence: Declare experimental/preview/supported/long-term/deprecated/removed tier, maintainer, profile support and unsupported services; target availability is not supported-tier promotion. Require actual typed MIR/effect/ownership/safety-preserving lowering, runtime/provider/capability limits, debug/stack/panic/spans, packaging/provenance/signature/SBOM and reproducible performance settings/device identity as applicable. Unsupported profiles reject with stable diagnostics; supported tiers run release-blocking conformance. Security-sensitive targets require GOV4; target retirement follows GOV8/GOV2 with explicit emergency exception only. Actual complete accepted artifact and consumer result for the named source contract, with input/source/policy/tool identity. Historical stage0 records or a passing schema alone do not implement these outcomes.\n\nRequired rejection evidence: Reject missing tier/owner/matrix, profile claims without fixtures, changed lowering semantics, hidden runtime/host authority and supported-tier claims missing debug/diagnostic/package/runtime tests. Reject unsupported performance claims, security-sensitive targets lacking review and removals bypassing compatibility/deprecation policy. Malformed/missing/stale/wrong-scope records and each named source rejection produce the original GOV diagnostics at the actual consuming boundary.\n\nDependencies: Profile/backend/runtime maintainers' actual conformance and unsupported-profile diagnostics; PKG3/7/10/11/12 package/provenance/target/signature/SBOM; TEST4/6/12/13 applicable reports; GOV2/GOV4/GOV8 decisions. Dependenci