rants remain separately typed contracts. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-explicit-family-selection-and-no-runtime-rejection - Selected runtime/provider service contracts and actual link/load/service-use evidence; pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products. Criterion profile-gap/meta/audited-implementation-provider (Open): Input: Meta raw-memory/FFI request with compiler implementation profile, declared compiler/provider grants and audited boundary/safe-wrapper metadata. Accept: Reject by default; admit only the explicitly allowed audited implementation-provider exception while keeping build hermeticity, scoped compiler access and generated target-profile/safety checking intact. Reject: Ambient host/FFI authority, unaudited or ungranted raw access, implementation-profile label used as an unconditional bypass and generated unsafe code without safety provenance. Required outputs: Implementation-profile/provider/audit decision and manifest, positive conditional-exception and negative default-denial fixtures, P3-COMPILER-CAPABILITY/GENERATED-SAFETY or relevant phase/source-origin diagnostics. Dependencies: auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime, plugins, runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping meta/audited-implementation-provider; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/native/profile-runtime-contract (Open): Input: Native namespace/function with selected managed/RC/ownership/region/arena/stack/static/foreign/pinned/device memory and runtime/allocator/scheduler/platform providers, including no-alloc regions. Accept: Check native source/runtime-service admission independently of memory-provider legality, record the selected runtime and memory strategy, and preserve no-alloc, safety and provider assumptions through lowering. No runtime beyond startup/ABI glue is a valid explicit choice. Reject: Hidden allocation in no-alloc code, GC assumed without provider, hidden hosted/reflection/eval/ambient services, raw memory in safe code, unsafe sharing/overflow and check erasure without proof. Required outputs: Native profile/memory/runtime/provider/allocation reports and accepted regime/no-runtime fixtures, missing-provider/hidden-service/no-alloc rejection and P5-ALLOC/MEMORY-PROVIDER/RUNTIME context. Dependencies: runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries, lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower1-validate-lowering-inputs, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping native/profile-runtime-contract; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. PERF9 deterministic-path admission: parse latency/jitter contract for function/module/interrupt/kernel/workflow/hardware path with target/workload, allocation/blocking, loop/recursion, interrupt/preemption/lock/provider assumptions and required failure mode. Emit latency manifest, loop/recursion/traversal/retry/timeout/queue bounds, allocation, blocking/lock/interrupt/preemption reports and static worst-case, bounded model/hardware or fingerprinted bounded empirical/hybrid evidence. Empirical evidence names clock/power/runtime/input/measurement conditions; average or percentile throughput alone is insufficient. Reject hidden GC/dynamic loading/reflection/unbounded allocation/locks/retries or unrecorded network/database/file/model/tool calls in deterministic paths unless isolated with noninterference proof or a profile-legal bounded provider. Runtime checks also need bounded cost. Reject optimization introducing unpredictable/unbounded tail latency and enforce reject-build when required latency is unproved/exceeded. Exercise valid bounds/provider/isolation and every missing/forbidden/exceeded case with PERF9 path/profile/target/budget/operation/span/proof/failure diagnostics. These are physical timing/representability constraints, not project work allowances. Decision criterion interface/core/runtime-free-values: Represent immutable core scalars/aggregates/persistent collections and typed pure errors without requiring a runtime or exposing concrete allocation identity; importing profiles select the representation. Reject: Reject raw addresses, finalizers, hidden managed runtime, allocation-location identity and host exceptions. Required outputs: Portable typed-core/profile manifest with no runtime-provider dependency and positive/negative representation-independence fixtures. Decision criterion interface/hosted/granted-services: Check hosted facility eligibility, effect allowance and capability authorization separately; narrow source/profile/package/provider/deployment policy and retain explicitly delegated host services. Reject: Reject ungranted reflection/eval/loading/process/secret use and raw MMIO/interrupt/kernel facilities; a hosted profile name grants no authority. Required outputs: Hosted profile/service/deployment manifests and effect/grant/forbidden-facility rejection diagnostics. Decision criterion interface/language/module/check-import-boundary: Check same-profile imports or explicit direct/facade/artifact-only boundaries against producer/consumer effects