     "- [ ] `legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/preserve-obligations-into-mir-and-runtime-execution` Preserve obligations into MIR and runtime execution\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Safety pipeline](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/c10_safety_analysis/pipeline.clj)\n\nClosing evidence: Surviving check/proof/source edges; missing-check and unjustified-elision rejection. For SAFE1/SAFE2/SAFE8/SAFE9/SAFE15, invalidate or regenerate affected facts after source, expansion, type/effect, profile/target, numeric mode, memory/capability provider, pass/backend, dependency, grant or replay changes. Verify imported certificate schema, exact inputs, compatibility and trust before use. Erase only the exact proved condition with surviving backend assumptions and recorded check/proof identities; restore the check or reject on invalidation. Manual review alone is insufficient unless governing claim policy explicitly permits it; authority, audit, replay and human-review gates retain their separate policy obligations. Criterion `runtime/check-proof-preservation`: Retain required bounds/numeric/initialization/alias/resource checks or applicable proof/trap/rejection evidence, including source/check identity and elision provenance. Accepted fixture: Preserve source/check identity and valid bounds/numeric/initialization/alias/resource proofs across lowering and runtime/target service boundaries. Negative fixture: On invalidation regenerate proof, retain the required check/trap or reject; reject proofless elision or lost policy evidence. Required evidence: check/proof/elision provenance and invalidation/rejection fixtures; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume mir/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/mir2-attach-fact-tables, lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower4-preserve-proofs-and-origins outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed. Decision allocation interface/safety/safe15/check-erasure (Open). Role: compiler safety-evidence maintainer. Erase a check only under its required valid evidence: proof of the exact dominated safety condition preserved through transformations and backend assumptions, and equivalent policy-artifact discharge where capability, effect, audit, replay or human-review checks require it. Record erased/residual check and evidence identities; regenerate evidence, retain checks or reject after invalidation. Policy gates never disappear merely for speed. Refusals and conditional cases: Reject erasure without a proven-safe source outcome, proof of the exact dominated condition valid after transformations and surviving backend assumptions, or required equivalent policy-artifact discharge for capability/effect/audit/replay/human-review gates. Record erased and residual checks and evidence IDs; regenerate evidence, retain checks or reject after invalidation. Speed alone never discharges policy. Required outputs: Check-erasure/residual-check record, exact condition/proof/backend assumption edges, policy discharge and invalidation/retention/rejection evidence. Consume actual dependency interface outputs: opt/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/opt3-protect-checks-and-anchors, lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower4-preserve-proofs-and-origins; whole-component completion is not a prerequisite. Retain exact source/compiler/pass/profile/target and checker/provider identities, actual positive products and refused-case diagnostics. Implementation acceptance remains unassessed. Allocation decision/domain-safe15-revoked-trust (Open). Role: legality compile-time safety/conformance checker. Input: the actual current dependency/consumer record and proposed older-to-current source field transpose. Required positive predicate: Preserve revoked-trust invalidation at the actual Domain/SAFE15 consumer when composing older facet bindings. Positive output witness: Current consumer proof/trust invalidation facts and a field-scoped transpose retaining every later source/context qualifier. Concrete negative case: An older Domain/SAFE15 binding restores certificate applicability after supporting trust/evidence was revoked or erases the dependent package/release qualification. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types5-integrate-typed-core supplies Actual typed core, ownership/layout and source-origin facts; effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects5-integrate-checked-core-consumers supplies Actual propagated effects and required capability facts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred. Allocation interface/safety/safe15/invalidation (Open). Role: legality compile-time safety/conformance checker. Input: subject-bound safety proof/certificate with assumptions, method/provider, trust and invalidation inputs. Required positive predicate: Invalidate/regenerate affected certificates across source, expansion, type/effect, profile/target/mode/provider/pass/backend/dependency/grant/replay changes and force rechecking when mappings cannot survive. Positive output witness: Assumption mapping, changed or revoked dependency invalidation, regenerated proof/restored check or rejection and downstream applicability. Concrete negative case: A certificate survives source/type/effect/profile/target/mode/provider/pass/backend/dependency/grant/replay changes or revoked supporting trust without rechecking. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types5-integrate-typed-core supplies Actual typed core, ownership/layout and source-origin facts; effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects5-integrate-checked-core-consumers supplies Actual propagated effects and required capability facts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred. Allocation interface/safety/safe8/atomic-ordering (Open). Role: legality compile-time safety/conformance checker. Input: task/shared-location/synchronization graph and selected target/provider memory model. Required positive predicate: Require explicit supported atomic order and fences, preserving it in optimization/lowering or diagnosing unsupported targets; unchecked target-specific atomics require audit. Positive output witness: Explicit atomic order/fence/target support and preserved optimization/lowering evidence. Concrete negative case: An atomic omits memory order, requires an unsupported target fence or lowering weakens acquire/release semantics. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types5-integrate-typed-core supplies Actual typed core, ownership/layout and source-origin facts; effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects5-integrate-checked-core-consumers supplies Actual propagated effects and required capability facts; runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred. SAFE1/SAFE9 preservation acceptance: Carry each operation's safety classification and source/generated-origin chain through expansion, analysis, MIR, optimization, lowering, emitted backend artifacts and linked dependencies; changed facts invalidate and recheck the affected obligation. Preserve declared numeric modes, rounding, NaN-sensitive comparisons, saturation and exceptions. Reject strict reassociation, reciprocal replacement without rounding-preserving proof, proofless check erasure and mismatched vector/target instructions unless the declared mode permits the change or actual checks guard the mismatch. Retain before/after classification, origin, numeric-contract and check/proof/guard records; exercise an accepted preserving transformation and each missing-origin, changed-mode, NaN, saturation, exception and invalidated-proof refusal. Consume Syntax/Expand origin records, MIR safety facts, Math resolved numeric contracts and Lower target/proof mappings as actual interface products, without requiring whole-component completion."},
