     "- [ ] `lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower1-validate-lowering-inputs` lower/1: Validate lowering inputs\n\nCurrent evidence/status: Open; partial source evidence above is not closure\n\nDone when (yes/no): Reject unverified/stale IR and incompatible profiles/features; expose explicit supported-operation and target matrices. P5: admit SIMD/intrinsics only with declared target features, numeric mode and alignment/layout evidence plus a valid fallback or rejection. A target wrapper does not justify unchecked intrinsics or change source legality; guarded variant selection and target lowering remain distinct interfaces. Foundation requirement gravity/multiversion-guard-manifest: For every dispatched backend variant emit target-feature guards, profile and numeric/safety constraints, fallback/rejection behavior and source-bound benchmark evidence; exercise each variant and guard failure. Refusals: Reject an unguarded unavailable instruction, widened profile, unjustified fast path, absent valid fallback or a benchmark from a different variant/target. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products; pass-evidence - Actual subject-bound checker/proof/certificate/audit/replay/test evidence and verdicts. Foundation requirement gravity/target-lowering-operation-contract: For every MIR/domain operation in the declared input closure emit its explicit accept/lower/delegate/reject disposition with target, profile, ABI/provider and preservation obligations, and consume that disposition at target emission. Refusals: Reject an uncovered operation, stale/unverified IR, unsupported feature