     "- [ ] `lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower4-preserve-proofs-and-origins` lower/4: Preserve proofs and origins\n\nCurrent evidence/status: Open; partial source evidence above is not closure\n\nDone when (yes/no): Map semantic proofs to target metadata only when assumptions hold, preserving source, safety and dependency records; reject proofless noalias/no-overflow/fast-math. Decision criterion interface/native/concurrency-order: Preserve declared task/thread/lock/message and atomic/fence ordering semantics and required provider/target facts through native lowering. Reject: Reject unsupported target order/atomic operations, detached invalid borrows, unsafe shared-state transformations and weakened ordering without lawful semantics. Required outputs: Native scheduler/atomic/lock/transfer and target-lowering records, ordering/lifetime preservation and unsupported-context refusals. Criterion `performance/target-intrinsic-map` (Open; implementation unassessed). Input: source-bound performance/target-intrinsic-map request and its declared profile/target/policy facts. Accept: Lower vector operations only through intrinsic maps binding required features, numeric mode, alignment, memory order, fallback and proof/certificate. Reject: Reject a map with absent features, mismatched numeric/alignment/memory-order assumptions, missing applicable proof or math certificate, or an unsupported target reachable without fallback or an execution-preventing guard. Required output: Source-operation to target-intrinsic map, required features, numeric mode, alignment, memory order, fallback and proof/certificate references; accepted lowering and guard/fallback rejection fixtures. Preserve the source facets, conditional rules, diagnostic context and dependencies pinned in this per-ID proposal. Dependencies consume actual outputs, not whole-task completion."},
