bounds/permission widening. Required outputs: Capability pointer/layout/metadata target manifest, legal derivation and rejected widening/representation fixtures, P8-CAPABILITY diagnostics identifying metadata field, module/signal/origin and target evidence. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types2-check-declared-abstractions, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, backend-hdl interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping hardware/capability-representation; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/hardware/capability-tag-paths (Open): Input: Every capability-bearing register, memory, DMA, FIFO, bus/bridge, debug and external-port path with target tag/metadata propagation or destruction declaration. Accept: Preserve tags and capability metadata on all declared carrying paths, or mark a tag-destroying boundary and diagnose unless source explicitly expects destruction; retain audited authority-boundary qualifications. Reject: Unmarked tag/metadata loss, silent ordinary-storage conversion and omitted path/target support evidence; explicit expected destruction is a qualified legal test case rather than an unconditional rejection. Required outputs: Tag-preservation/path report and capability-bearing interface manifests; preserving, marked-destruction, explicitly-expected-destruction and unmarked-loss fixtures with P8-TAG path/origin/target context. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types2-check-declared-abstractions, lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower1-validate-lowering-inputs, backend-hdl interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping hardware/capability-tag-paths; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/hardware/clock-reset-contract (Open): Input: Hardware registers/state with clock domain and reset sync/async, active level, value and affected-register declarations. Accept: Assign each register a domain and defined reset or explicitly uninitialized state; require a hardware audit for unsafe/unspecified power-on behavior and preserve the accepted declaration into clock/reset/timing records. Reject: Missing/invalid domain or reset, undeclared power-on behavior and lost initialization evidence. Required outputs: Clock/reset-domain and initialization reports, accepted declared-uninitialized/audited-power-on cases, rejected missing-clock/reset cases and P8-CLOCK/RESET diagnostics. Dependencies: legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, backend-hdl interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping hardware/clock-reset-contract; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/hardware/compartment-boundary (Open): Input: Capability-hardware compartment crossing with compartment IDs, sealed entry/call gates, call/return authority, bounded shared state and transferred-capability lifetime/revocation assumptions. Accept: Validate the explicit authority transfer, legal entry and return paths and permitted sharing/lifetime assumptions at each crossing. Reject: Implicit sharing through wires/debug/untyped maps, undeclared entry or return authority, invalid sealed state and omitted shared-memory/lifetime rules. Required outputs: Compartment/authority-transfer and temporal-assumption report, sealed-entry/call/return/shared-state positive/negative cases and P8-COMPARTMENT boundary/origin/metadata diagnostics. Dependencies: legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, backend-hdl interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping hardware/compartment-boundary; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/hardware/external-port-contract (Open): Input: Hardware port or bus with direction, fixed width, protocol/ready-valid behavior, timing, reset and capability boundary; tag lanes/metadata permissions for capability-bearing interfaces. Accept: Validate the complete external protocol and target shape, allowed permission transitions, compartment status and debug/DMA/bridge capability-observation/destruction rules; preserve interface source/target metadata. Reject: Untyped/incomplete ports, protocol violations, missing timing/reset/capability evidence and undeclared metadata destruction or authority transfer. Required outputs: Port/bus/interface manifest, protocol acceptance/rejection fixtures and P8-PORT/capability diagnostics with signal/module/domain/origin/target context. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types2-check-declared-abstractions, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, backend-hdl interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping hardware/external-port-contract; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/hardware/state-machine-contract (Open): Input: Hardware state-machine declaration with state type, initial state, transition function, inputs/outputs, reset, illegal-state behavior and required coverage/assertion hooks. Accep