     "- [ ] `release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/bind-each-claimed-component-to-exact-implementation-and-conformance` Bind each claimed component to exact implementation and conformance\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Overall roadmap](../../docs/implementation-roadmap.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Component outcome receipts, positive/negative programs and explicit unsupported surface. Maintain the source-bound task/disposition matrix for all 240 original contracts and the separately declared release and Platform Product extensions. Keep every missing producer/checker/consumer interface, alias or split question, and architecture choice as finite named remaining work with criteria, dependencies and accountable role; an accountability link does not establish an implementation interface. Resolve those decisions and bind actual component evidence before claiming the corresponding release scope. This release-claim obligation does not block ordinary semantic development. Foundation requirement gravity/coverage-claim-slice: Publish each domain coverage claim as an exact behavior slice with source forms, profile, target/backend, provider/runtime assumptions, emitted artifacts and explicit unsupported boundaries, linked to the actual demonstrating product. Refusals: Reject a whole-domain claim supported only by a smaller slice, a missing profile/target, or a provider adapter presented as a complete replacement. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products. Foundation requirement gravity/coverage-claim-status-distinction: Classify every declared coverage entry as implemented, designed, delegated, experimental, unsupported or out of scope with its concrete source/evidence basis; expose the classification to consumers of the claim. Refusals: Reject promoting a designed/delegated/example-only entry to implemented, silently dropping unsupported entries or treating absent evidence as out of scope. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Foundation requirement gravity/coverage-positive-negative-fixtures: For each claimed domain slice retain real accepted and rejected input fixtures with expected artifacts and structured owning diagnostics, executed through the claimed implementation/provider boundary. Refusals: Reject coverage evidence missing either accepted execution or the relevant invalid-input refusal; synthetic model agreement and a catalogue name alone cannot close the slice. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products; diag/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/integrate-runtimebuildeditor-consumers-without-rule-drift - Actual runtime/compiler/tool structured diagnostics with stable owning codes and provenance. Foundation requirement gravity/documentation-lock-scope: Assess the explicit D2 M0 forty-document documentation lock against each of its five named exit gates, retaining the exact document set, source hashes, reviewed results and unresolved gate failures; label the decision documentation-only. Refusals: Reject a lock missing any named document or gate, stale source evidence, or an attempt to turn that documentation decision into executable compiler, milestone or release acceptance. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Foundation requirement gravity/foundation-semantic-change-control: For a changed foundation guarantee publish the affected D0-D9 and downstream contract set, compatibility decision, changed conformance fixtures and evidence invalidations before claiming the changed support. Refusals: Reject a semantic change without affected-contract review, stale acceptance reuse or omitted compatibility/fixture updates; the policy record is not actual approval of the change. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): tools/finite-service-outcomes-and-remaining-work/lint-analysis-tool-maintainer - Canonical D3 vocabulary/layer maps and source/manifest terminology check results; pass-evidence - Actual subject-bound checker/proof/certificate/audit/replay/test evidence and verdicts. Foundation requirement gravity/migration-provenance-safety: For a generated/migrated replacement slice preserve incumbent/source/generator provenance, recheck generated code and unsafe audit boundaries, and record the scoped conformance and performance evidence needed before retiring its interop path. Refusals: Reject interop retirement on translation success alone, missing provenance/audits or unexplained behavioral/performance differences; preserve policy-qualified narrowed and unsupported cases. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-safe-code-classification-and-taintunsafe-boundaries - Dangerous-operation outcomes, actual checks, proof references and audited wrapper boundaries; pass-evidence - Actual subject-bound checker/proof/certificate/audit/replay/test evidence and verdicts. Foundation requirement gravity/milestone-contract-sequencing: Bind each milestone claim to its governing upstream contracts and actual declared interface products in D2 order; record early downstream work as a supported interface experiment with explicit non-release scope. Refusals: Reject downstream support claims without required upstream contracts or evidence; do not block ordinary isolated development merely because a different component is incomplete. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products. Foundation requirement gravity/milestone-evidence-bundle: Assemble the D2 milestone bundle for the exact claimed surface: governing document versions, real accepted/rejected programs, diagnostics, emitted artifacts, profile/target matrices, safety/trust boundaries, reproducibility and open risks. Refusals: Reject a bundle with an omitted required member, stale input identity, unsupported matrix cell or concealed open risk; a document inventory is not an executable bundle. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/close-reproducibility-and-target-matrix - Locked source/compiler/provider/target build graph and canonical rebuild comparison; pass-evidence - Actual subject-bound checker/proof/certificate/audit/replay/test evidence and verdicts. Foundation requirement gravity/milestone-executable-evidence: Before marking a milestone complete execute its required positive and negative programs through the claimed compiler/runtime path and bind real emitted products and owning diagnostics to the milestone decision. Refusals: Reject milestone completion supported only by plans, schemas, mocked execution, a passing unrelated helper or missing rejection evidence. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products; cli/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/connect-checkruncompilebuildtestpackageverify-to-real-services - Actual source-to-public-command execution, declared stdout authority and outputs; lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower5-integrate-target-emission - Actual target emission artifacts and unsupported-feature diagnostics. Foundation requirement gravity/real-domain-coverage-evidence: Demonstrate the declared domain's actual constraints, integration boundary and produced artifact on a representative real workload, with required rejection cases and an explicit supported subset. Refusals: Reject replacing the required domain behavior with a toy simulation, mock provider, catalogue entry or unrelated subset; simulator evidence is allowed only where the owning contract permits that specific substitute. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products; pass-evidence - Actual subject-bound checker/proof/certificate/audit/replay/test evidence and verdicts. Foundation requirement gravity/release-matrix-evidence: Bind each milestone/release claim to a versioned profile-by-target/backend/runtime matrix whose claimed cells each link exact accepted/rejected executable evidence and unsupported cells remain explicit. Refusals: Reject a cell supported by another profile/target's receipt, stale compiler/provider inputs or a missing required negative fixture; one cell cannot imply whole-matrix support. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/close-reproducibility-and-target-matrix - Locked source/compiler/provider/target build graph and canonical rebuild comparison; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products. Foundation requirement gravity/replacement-parity-evidence: Before upgrading a named interop slice to replacement status compare actual incumbent and Gravity behavior, diagnostics, effects/capabilities, artifacts and applicable performance on the declared workload, with reviewed deltas and limits. Refusals: Reject replacement promotion from a shim, translation result or toy fixture alone, unexplained divergence or performance evidence from another scope. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/close-reproducibility-and-target-matrix - Locked source/compiler/provider/target build graph and canonical rebuild comparison; pass-evidence - Actual subject-bound checker/proof/certificate/audit/replay/test evidence and verdicts. Foundation requirement gravity/replacement-slice-record: Publish a versioned replacement-slice record identifying incumbent behavior, actual Gravity source and explicitly preserved, narrowed, delegated and unsupported operations with profile/target/provider and migration provenance. Refusals: Reject a replacement claim omitting a known narrowed/unsupported behavior, silently treating a delegated operation as native replacement or losing the incumbent comparison basis. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products. D5 replacement parity also compares safety, packaging and tooling on the named incumbent and Gravity slice and records migration feasibility. Name each applicable parity dimension, its actual fixture/artifact and any reviewed narrower/delegated result; reject an omitted applicable safety, packaging or tooling comparison or a replacement claim whose migration path is not supported by the recorded boundaries. Tool/compiler consistency alone is not incumbent tooling parity."},
