     "- [ ] `release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-stage-compatibilityequivalence-across-the-claimed-compiler` Complete stage compatibility/equivalence across the claimed compiler\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Equivalence contract](../../docs/phase-15-bootstrap-and-self-hosting/209-boot7-self-hosting-validation-and-equivalence-plan.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Fresh stage-to-stage outputs and diagnostics, residual trusted-code inventory BOOT1/BOOT3/BOOT5/BOOT7: Publish a versioned row for every claimed stage and authoritative module revision, naming source/compiler/artifact identities, supported and unsupported documents/features/profiles/backends/runtime/package/library/test closure, owned or deferred gaps, conformance links and release eligibility. Record exact compiler-module ownership and residual TCB with measurable migration delta. Compare both named compilers and canonical artifacts under declared applicable hash/manifest/diagnostic/conformance/runtime/IR/performance/accepted-delta modes; preserve stable codes/spans and provenance. Reject missing outputs, implicit inherited support, omitted stage rows, unsupported claims, stale matrix versions and unexplained drift; accept deltas only with policy-linked review. Performance bounds apply only when performance is part of acceptance; no compiler work quota is introduced. Execute the intermediate authoritative stage/module admission decision against this exact candidate and declared subset, consuming the fresh conformance, equivalence/accepted-delta, matrix, provenance, TCB and applicable audit records. Record admit or deny with candidate/source/compiler/artifact identities and failed predicates. Deny failing applicable suites, stale or missing required evidence, unexplained drift, unsupported claimed support and missing ownership/matrix updates. Exercise both a valid intermediate admission and each refusal. Retain explicitly owned/deferred gaps outside the claimed subset; final release policy separately rejects unreviewed gaps for claimed release support. This decision does not produce the evidence it consumes, replace final release acceptance, or gate ordinary semantic development. Foundation requirement gravity/bootstrap-equivalence-before-retirement: Before retiring a named seed component, compare the declared predecessor and Gravity successor stages on accepted and rejected programs, canonical outputs and diagnostics; record residual TCB and an explicit retirement decision for that component only. Refusals: Deny retirement for missing stage products, unreviewed drift, stale compiler/source identities or required conformance failures; an intermediate stage admission cannot retire unrelated seed components. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products; build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/close-reproducibility-and-target-matrix - Locked source/compiler/provider/target build graph and canonical rebuild comparison. Foundation requirement gravity/bootstrap-staged-trust-reduction: Record each actual compiler/platform component migration into Gravity with source and predecessor/successor compiler identities, reproducible stage products, exact supported subset and the measured residual seed/TCB inventory. Refusals: Reject a claimed seed reduction without an actual migrated product or with missing lineage; plans, supplied success labels and one migrated helper cannot establish complete seed absence. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products; build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/close-reproducibility-and-target-matrix - Locked source/compiler/provider/target build graph and canonical rebuild comparison. Source compiler/c1/self-hosting-comparison: Represent compiler structures as Gravity values and expose comparable public stage artifacts across seed and self-hosted implementations, even with optimized private layouts. Concrete acceptance: Compare actual seed and next-stage public artifacts for the same module; missing public stage output, an unrepresentable compiler structure, unexplained semantic drift or a provenance mismatch fails even when private layouts differ legitimately. Retain actual input/output and diagnostic identities plus positive and rejected-case artifacts; supplied success flags, proposal delivery and broad parent links are not executable evidence. Bootstrap criterion bootstrap/stage-equivalence: Actually compare outputs of both named compiler artifacts on pinned source/compiler/stdlib/conformance inputs using every comparison mode declared applicable for that stage: hash, canonical manifest, diagnostic, conformance, runtime output, IR modulo IDs, conditional performance and reviewed accepted-delta. Identify compared artifacts, inputs, outputs, canonicalization and applicable stage support level; emit a provenance-bound equivalence report linked from bootstrap provenance with diagnostic, IR, conformance and accepted/rejected difference records. Fail missing compiler identity/output, unexplained artifact or diagnostic drift, unreviewed or policy-unlinked deltas, failing supported-feature conformance and performance regression beyond a declared acceptance bound when performance is applicable. Preserve stable codes/source spans; permitted metadata/timestamp/wording differences require the declared reviewed comparison policy and cannot hide semantic drift. Retain BOOT1004/BOOT3003/BOOT6003 and BOOT7001-BOOT7007, and exercise both a valid comparison and each applicable refusal. Comparison does not produce compiler executables or independently admit intermediate migration/final release. Required outputs: actual stage comparison inputs/outputs and equivalence artifact; diagnostic/IR/conformance and accepted-delta reports; missing-output/drift/unreviewed-delta/conformance/conditional-performance negative fixtures."},
