     "- [ ] `runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/finish-managednative-execution-startup-panic-and-cleanup` Finish managed/native execution, startup, panic and cleanup\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Development evaluator](../../bootstrap/gravity/src/gravity/runtime.gravity) and [native manifest](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/bootstrap_impl/components/foundation/00287-minimal-native-runtime-manifest.clj)\n\nClosing evidence: Executed startup/failure/resource fixtures and manifest-to-service agreement; before user code, validate selected provider existence, artifact versions, grant scopes, compiled contracts, profile/target compatibility and enabled safety/audit requirements; reject a missing required provider unless a declared fallback applies, with positive fallback and negative mismatch fixtures under [L15 runtime providers](../../docs/phase-01-core-language/025-l15-capability-provider-specification.md) . R1/R3/R4: typed host adapters with effects, capabilities, taint, error and source-map contracts; selected host/version/module/collection/dynamic-state manifests; startup, initialization, handoff and teardown order; explicit panic/trap/abort/unwind/result policy; host null/undefined conversion, exception and rejected-promise translation; Gravity equality/hashing/serialization conformance; deterministic linear cleanup independent of process exit or GC. Reject undeclared helper effects, untranslated/null foreign values and GC-only linear cleanup; debug services must be absent or release-policy marked. Dependencies: Lower supplies ABI and source maps, Legality supplies legal services, and Auth supplies grants; selected compiler services do not close all managed/native targets. P4: execute deterministic cleanup for linear host resources despite GC; managed objects remain GC-managed and only an explicit boundary can rely on finalizer timing. Reject GC-only cleanup where deterministic release is required; preserve exactly-once flow evidence from Legality separately from executed terminal operations. Translate host errors through the declared Gravity failure channel with source/generated origins. Residual criterion runtime/debug-service-selection: Select debug services explicitly for each native/managed runtime and release policy. Show a debug artifact and release artifact whose service/helper manifests expose exactly the selected stack/allocation/check/trace hooks; debug-only services are absent in release unless policy explicitly allows and marks them. Preserve source/check/allocation/provider/lifetime/release identity and proof-elision metadata. Stack diagnostics are capability-neutral unless an external lookup is enabled: reject undeclared filesystem, environment, network or symbol-server access, unmarked debug services and lost source/provenance; required safety checks cannot disappear with debug instrumentation. Provider debug manifests retain profile support, allocation effects, layout/alignment, failure/lifetime/deallocation strategy and unsafe boundaries; traces retain allocation site, resource ID and release site, including selected borrow-debug checks. Enforce sink grants and redact secrets, credentials, prompts, model outputs, user/tainted inputs, raw memory, environment values, package tokens, database rows and deployment identifiers; local logging permission cannot authorize network telemetry. Residual criterion runtime/managed-collection-semantics: For each claimed managed host/version and collection implementation, execute Gravity-observable value/collection fixtures for host representation, nullability, equality, hashing, serialization, mutability, identity and taint. Emit the managed-value/collection manifest and source-bound comparison results for persistent values adapted from host collections or implemented by Gravity. Reject observable host equality/hash/serialization/mutation behavior that diverges from the declared Gravity contract, unchecked nulls and a collection implementation missing from the host manifest; host convenience cannot define portable core meaning. Residual criterion runtime/managed-dynamic-state: Manifest dynamic variables, thread-local values, async context, namespace loading, REPL state and hot reload for the selected host/version/module system. Show declared binding/context behavior through thread and async boundaries and namespace/session changes, retaining source maps, taint, error translation and resource policy. Reject unmanifested state, ambient host reflection/eval/dynamic import/package globals without effects/grants and hosted dynamic state leaking into a lower profile without a legal facade/artifact. Session state influencing build artifacts is captured or nonhermetic, not an implicit capability. Residual criterion runtime/managed-null-conversion: At each claimed host adapter, manifest host/Gravity representation and nullability and convert host null or undefined through the selected Option, Result, checked-wrapper or opaque-foreign-value contract. Execute null, undefined and non-null fixtures for that declared boundary, retaining taint, errors and source/generated-origin diagnostics. Reject unchecked host null/undefined entering a safe Gravity value, a conversion inconsistent with its Gravity type or a missing adapter/null policy; an opaque foreign value does not authorize unchecked access or leakage into lower profiles. Alternative conversion policies are conditional choices, not a requirement to apply every conversion to one value. Exception/null boundary fixtures also reject untranslated host exceptions or rejected promises and preserve the declared Gravity error/panic/effect channel. Criterion profile-gap/hosted/deterministic-resource-cleanup (Open): Input: Hosted managed objects and linear file/socket/lock/transaction resources under declared rooting/finalizer and Gravity cleanup contracts. Accept: Check exactly-once linear resource flow and separately execute required deterministic terminal cleanup despite host GC; permit managed object lifetime and explicit boundary finalizer behavior without turning all objects into linear resources. Reject: GC-only release for resources requiring deterministic cleanup, missing/double terminal operations, invalid failure-path ownership transfer and reliance on unspecified finalizer timing. Required outputs: Resource-flow and executed cleanup records for success/failure/transfer, host-boundary lifecycle metadata and P4-RESOURCE origin/effect/grant/host-policy diagnostics. Dependencies: runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping hosted/deterministic-resource-cleanup; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Source obligation `language/effects/interpret-resumable-error`: Interpret typed resumable error payloads and resume values while preserving abort and cleanup paths. Accept: Interpret typed error/resume payloads and values, including normal resume, abort and cleanup exits; retain original effect label, handler identity and declared continuation mode. Reject: Reject unsafe resume, request/response mismatch, resume after finalization, invalid captured resources and undeclared handler effects or grants. Required outputs: Typed error-handler contract, resume/abort/cleanup ordering traces and positive/negative continuation diagnostics. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime, runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Source obligation `language/errors/execute-defined-check-failure`: Give a retained runtime safety check a specified typed failure or profile-defined trap instead of undefined behavior. Accept: For each retained bounds/initialization/numeric/capability/taint/replay check, emit the specified typed failure or profile-defined trap according to runtime and safety mode, with its check and source identity. Reject: Reject an unspecified failure outcome or target undefined behavior substituted for the check's required failure path. Required outputs: Check-to-failure/trap table, triggered-check fixtures, typed failure records and matching profile/runtime/safety diagnostics. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Source obligation `language/errors/lower-panic`: Lower an unrecoverable panic according to the active profile, preserving source/artifact provenance when possible and rejecting panic as ordinary stable-API control flow. Accept: Emit the selected profile's panic lowering: hosted exception/task abort, native runtime handler, kernel trap/platform path, firmware reset/halt, hardware synthesis-time unreachable/trap artifact or runtime-panic rejection, distributed failure state and AI policy/orchestration record. Preserve source/artifact provenance when available and declare try/throw lowering or rejection. Reject: Reject panic as ordinary stable-API control flow, an unsupported lowering or an undeclared profile failure path; report L9-PANIC-PROFILE. Required outputs: Profile-specific panic/error lowering matrix, target failure artifacts, positive/negative fixtures and provenance-linked diagnostics. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open."},
