     "- [ ] `runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries` Implement memory, concurrency and typed FFI boundaries\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Runtime contracts](../../docs/phase-08-runtime-architecture/README.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Allocation, lifetime, transfer, race and foreign-failure conformance with explicit providers. Execute the [SAFE2-SAFE8 contracts](../../docs/phase-02-safety/README.md): declared allocation and cleanup failures, partial initialization cleanup, region/arena generation and borrow checks, release through the correct allocator/provider, callback lifetime/thread/reentrancy/release and foreign error/exception/promise translation. Reject retained borrows, post-reset access, missing FFI declarations, unsupported atomics and unsynchronized mutable access; validate immutable sharing, lock cleanup, actor/channel transfer and declared backpressure/cancellation. Inspect actual checks and audit records, with no hidden GC or host-thread fallback. . R3/R5/R6/R10: allocation/deallocation/provider manifests, no-allocation and region/arena escape rejection, linear acquire/transfer/consume ledgers, device address-space/transfer/synchronization/lifetime checks, audited raw-memory wrappers, and agreement of retained checks with exact proof-elision records; atomics with target memory order/scope/alignment, structured task parent or explicit lifecycle owner, cancellation cleanup and failure propagation, actor/channel schemas with ordering/backpressure/transfer policy; FFI symbol/loading policy, ABI/layout conformance, null/handle/lifetime/ownership/error adapters and callbacks re-entering capability/taint/thread-affinity/scheduler checks. Reject mismatched providers, races, orphan tasks, unsupported atomics, schemaless messages, raw extern safe calls and invalid callback entry. Dependencies: ownership and Legality supply compile-time facts, Lower supplies target layouts, Auth supplies grants, and distributed execution supplies replay policy; runtime debug checks cannot substitute for compile-time safety. P4/P5: host-object/native FFI records bind runtime/version/symbol, Gravity and foreign types, rooting/ownership/lifetime, nullability, failure mapping, affinity, ABI, effects/grants and safe wrappers. Insufficient host metadata permits opaque provider-only handles, not unrestricted manipulation; raw native imports are not directly safe-callable. Exercise positive boundaries and missing metadata, ungranted call, invalid lifetime and untranslated failure rejection. Residual criterion runtime/foreign-symbol-resolution: Resolve a declared foreign symbol and dynamically load an admitted library/module only under package/deployment policy, the named provider/library/version identity and required effects/grants. Emit the binding, symbol-resolution and generated-adapter records tied to target ABI, calling convention, layout/alignment and source/unsafe audit. Positive fixtures resolve the admitted identity through its safe wrapper/provider; negative fixtures reject wrong/missing symbols, mismatched ABI/layout/provider identity and ungranted or policy-denied dynamic loading. Resolution/loading does not bypass nullability, lifetime/ownership, callback affinity/taint or foreign error conversion contracts. Preserve the delivered split between resolution and loading as two criteria within this same task, without accepting an alias or retiring their history. Foundation requirement gravity/interop-boundary-manifest: Produce and consume the typed foreign boundary manifest with applicable ABI/layout, ownership/transfer/lifetime, null/error/callback/thread, host/schema/provider, effects/grants and provenance obligations; demonstrate a conforming boundary invocation. Refusals: Reject a missing applicable obligation, incompatible ABI/schema/provider, invalid ownership transfer or absent authority; a declaration-only check does not prove actual conversion or callback execution. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): schema - Versioned source schema, generated validators/codecs and parity artifacts; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products. Foundation requirement gravity/interop-is-not-host-semantics: Normalize an admitted foreign value/failure/callback through its declared typed and audited Gravity boundary while preserving Gravity errors, source identity, effects and capability requirements. Refusals: Reject a host null, exception, reflection/loading convention or object-identity assumption leaking into portable Gravity semantics; keep actual adaptation separate from manifest publication. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products; diag/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/integrate-runtimebuildeditor-consumers-without-rule-drift - Actual runtime/compiler/tool structured diagnostics with stable owning codes and provenance. Criterion profile-gap/hosted/typed-object-boundary (Open): Input: Host object boundary with runtime/version, symbol/class/module/member, Gravity/host type, rooting/ownership/lifetime, exception translation, affinity, effects/grants and source-map support. Accept: Emit and validate typed schema/protocol/foreign-handle boundaries before manipulation; insufficient metadata yields opaque values operated only through declared provider APIs. Reject: Untyped host object use, missing lifecycle/affinity/grant metadata and unnormalized host failures crossing into Gravity. Required outputs: Host interop/object/runtime dependency and deployment-capability manifests, typed-versus-opaque boundary fixtures, P4-HOST-OBJECT/EXCEPTION/CROSS-IMPORT and effect/grant diagnostics. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types2-check-declared-abstractions, schema, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping hosted/typed-object-boundary; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/native/ffi-boundary (Open): Input: Native foreign import/call with ABI/calling convention, link symbol, type mapping, ownership transfer/lifetime/nullability, failure/affinity, effects/grants and safe-wrapper or unsafe contract. Accept: Validate the complete foreign boundary, execute the admitted call through the wrapper, and separately translate declared foreign failures into Gravity; preserve ABI/source/provider identity and every safe-wrapper precondition. Reject: Raw import called directly from safe code, incomplete ABI/ownership/error metadata, missing grant, invalid lifetime/nullability/affinity and untranslated failure or unaudited raw memory. Required outputs: Native ABI/FFI/safety manifests and admitted/rejected call/failure fixtures with P5-FFI/RAW-MEMORY diagnostics identifying ABI/provider/effect/grant/source/generated origin. Dependencies: legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks, lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower1-validate-lowering-inputs, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping native/ffi-boundary; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Source obligation `language/concurrency/execute-owned-actor-message`: Execute typed/effect-visible actor messages against actor-owned state, preserving scheduler/failure assumptions and explicit durable schema/replay boundaries. Accept: Execute typed, effect-visible messages against actor-owned state with explicit capability requirements, scheduler assumptions and failure behavior. A durable actor/service boundary carries schema/artifact identity and replay records. Reject: Reject state access outside actor ownership, untyped or undeclared-effect messages, missing required grants and durable delivery without schema/replay evidence. Required outputs: Actor state/message schemas, scheduler/failure manifest, ownership/effect/grant decisions and durable replay/denial traces. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime, runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/connect-distributedai-replay-and-interactive-execution; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Source obligation `language/effects/interpret-async-suspension`: Interpret typed async suspend/await operations with scheduler wakeup, cancellation and timeout behavior admitted by the active profile. Accept: Interpret typed async suspend/await, scheduler wakeup, cancellation and timeout operations only for a profile/runtime supporting the handler and resume mode; preserve handler identity, original labels, residual effects and required grants. Reject: Reject request/response/result mismatch, unsupported scheduler/profile, missing authority, resume after cancel/completion or illegal captured lifetime. Required outputs: Typed handler/runtime contract, suspend/wakeup/await/cancel/timeout traces, cleanup records and stable rejection diagnostics. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Source obligation `language/effects/interpret-generator`: Interpret typed generator yield/send/completion and close operations under the handler's declared resume mode. Accept: Execute typed yield, send, completion and close operations under the declared generator resume mode; retain original labels, handler identity, captures and profile/grant facts. Reject: Reject wrong send/completion types, unsafe or repeated affine resumes, resume after close and unsupported profile/capture transfer. Required outputs: Generator request/result/continuation records and accepted yield/send/complete/close plus rejected unsafe-resume fixtures. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Source obligation `language/errors/normalize-foreign-failure`: Normalize a foreign/host call's error, exception, null and failure-resource behavior into an explicit typed Gravity boundary contract before entering safe/non-null source semantics. Accept: Before safe/non-null entry, convert nullable/undefined foreign values through the declared Option/Result, checked-wrapper or opaque-foreign-value contract; declared nullable Option absence may produce None without inventing an error. Separately translate foreign/host error returns, errno-like state, exceptions, panics, rejected promises, signals and exit statuses into declared typed Gravity error contracts. Do not convert a real error or capability denial into absence. Retain host/foreign type identity, ownership transfer on failure, cleanup, abort policy, runtime dependencies and exception/null contracts for hosted dispatch. Reject: Reject an unexpected or undeclared null, null crossing a non-null type, untranslated/untyped foreign failure and a missing mapping or failure-resource contract; report P4-EXCEPTION, L8-HOST-DISPATCH, L9-HOST-ERROR/L9-FFI-ERROR or L19-ERROR-MAP as applicable. Required outputs: Foreign/host dispatch and error-mapping artifacts, hosted conformance, failure-cleanup tests and diagnostics with host/runtime, source/generated origin, requested effect, grant, symbol and deployment policy when relevant. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/finish-managednative-execution-startup-panic-and-cleanup, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime, types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types4-preserve-and-invalidate-facts; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Source obligation `language/memory/release-provider-storage`: Release or transfer a provider-managed/foreign/linear allocation according to lifetime, finalization and matching allocator identity, rejecting leaks, double release and incompatible release operations. Accept: Release or transfer provider/foreign/linear storage under declared destruction/finalization and exactly-once rules. Match allocator identity with a compatible release operation; preserve transfer direction, borrowed lifetime, nullability, initialization, errors, thread affinity and callback lifetime. Unexpressible foreign facts require an unsafe boundary or checked wrapper. Reject: Reject leaks, double release, incompatible allocator/releaser and a safe binding missing ownership/lifetime/nullability/allocator facts; report L18-LEAK, L18-DOUBLE-RELEASE or L18-FFI-ALLOCATOR. Required outputs: Provider/foreign allocation-release and ownership records, leak/exactly-once/allocator-mismatch fixtures, checked-wrapper or unsafe-policy evidence and diagnostics. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime, types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types4-preserve-and-invalidate-facts; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Decision criterion `interface/runtime/check-allocation-provider-policy` (Open): Before selecting or using an allocation provider, check that its family, effects, layout/alignment, lifetime, failure and release contract satisfies the namespace/profile/target memory policy. Refuse: Reject wrong provider family, undeclared effects, incompatible layout/lifetime/failure or release behavior before allocation; this is a semantic provider check, not a compiler work allowance. Required outputs: allocation-provider selection/admission manifest and compatibility/failure/release refusal fixtures. Dependencies consume auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks as typed operation artifacts, not whole-component completion. Preserve every source facet and unresolved metadata ID in the exact phase-09 decision allocation; no implementation acceptance is inferred. Decision criterion interface/runtime/concurrency-memory-order: For every selected atomic/lock/thread/scheduler provider execute the declared operation, memory order, synchronization scope, alignment and target support under accepted race/ownership evidence. Emit operation/provider/target records and synchronization/transfer traces; accept representable supported synchronization and reject unsupported orders/scopes, misalignment, unprotected shared mutation and undeclared host-thread fallback. Compile-time race evidence remains required independently of debug checks. Decision criterion interface/runtime/typed-message-delivery: Deliver channel/actor messages under declared schemas/versions, ownership transfers, ordering/delivery guarantees, mailbox/backpressure, cancellation and failure policies for the selected scheduler/transport. Emit actual transfer and receive traces with source/context/authority and schema validation; accept isolated/owned messages and reject schemaless/mismatched messages, illegal shared mutation, invalid transfer/lifetime and unsupported blocking/ordering behavior. Durable transports retain event-log/idempotency/compensation and migration/replay records; no hidden host scheduler or ambient network grant is implied. Decision criterion interface/runtime/task-lifecycle: Execute tasks under the declared scheduler with a parent scope or explicit lifecycle owner, validated captures/ownership transfers, result/failure propagation, timeout, cancellation and deterministic cleanup. Emit task-tree, ownership-transfer, cancellation/failure and cleanup traces. Reject orphaned or lifecycle-less tasks, incompatible capture/transfer, missing cleanup or worker/job policy with the owning R6-TASK/R6-CANCEL/DOM8-JOB diagnostics. Preserve R7 failure-policy and Behavior A4 ownership; scheduler availability grants no missing authority or policy. Source recovery preserves full owning clause context and requires independent current-composition review; implementation remains Open. Decision criterion interface/runtime/device-memory-transfer: Enforce declared device address space, ownership/lifetime, transfer completion, visibility, aliasing and synchronization at actual provider transfer boundaries. Reject: Reject use-after-release, double release, premature host visibility and missing/incompatible transfer/barrier evidence; retain every unresolved finite18 facet ID for authentic index recovery. Required outputs: Device transfer/lifetime/synchronization manifest, legal/illegal transfer traces and source-index adjudication restoring real metadata for the retained unresolved IDs."},
