     "- [ ] `runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/connect-distributedai-replay-and-interactive-execution` Connect distributed/AI replay and interactive execution\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Runtime contracts](../../docs/phase-08-runtime-architecture/README.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Recorded nondeterminism, replay equality, no undeclared duplicated external effect, REPL grant denial. R6/R7/R8/R9: topology/provider/event-log/state/message schemas; durable idempotency, timeout/retry/cancellation/failure/compensation records; migration or rejection of replay-incompatible code/topology/schema changes; model/provider/prompt provenance, output and sink validation, policy-recorded provider substitution, typed tool contracts with caller/callee grants and policy-required human review, memory/retrieval privacy/retention/deletion/taint controls and secret redaction; R7/R8 replay-required segments return recorded model/tool/retrieval/memory/review decisions or reject a missing record. R6 concurrency fixtures accept an authorized graph-declared replay-safe repetition where no R7/R8 recorded-output obligation applies; the declaration never grants authority or overrides those recorded-output obligations. Interactive forms and generated code pass the ordinary compiler checks before execution; session manifests, transcripts, evaluated forms, syntax/core/MIR/source snapshots capture build-affecting state or mark nonhermeticity, and hot reload invalidates stale analysis/backend/runtime/package outputs. Reject undeclared repeated external calls, live nondeterministic calls in R7/R8 recorded-output segments even with a replay-safe graph declaration, repetitions without required authority, unvalidated trusted sinks, forbidden-profile eval, hidden interactive IO and stale reload artifacts. Dependencies: Domains supplies agent/workflow contracts, Schema supplies validators/migrations, Build consumes session inputs and invalidation, Auth supplies grants and review policy. Project work/token/call/time/retry allowances are removed admission requirements; actual provider billing/account limits remain external, and semantic failure/cancellation policy remains required. R8 mixed budget spans retain unresolved qualification in the family proposal.. Under [SAFE8/SAFE13](../../docs/phase-02-safety/README.md), retain signal/timer/retry/idempotency/compensation and tool failure records; exact replay consumes recorded model/tool outputs, while audit policy retains digests, schemas, decisions, review events and providers. None is allowed only in interactive or non-safe contexts; workflow and release claims require replay or audit. Execute retention/deletion and secret-tainted memory denial fixtures through the declared provider; prompt text never grants authority. Residual criterion runtime/hot-reload-invalidation: For a changed interactive definition, record changed source, affected namespace/dependency edges and invalidation of stale syntax, analysis, typed core, MIR/domain IR, backend, runtime and package artifacts. Emit a hot-reload/session record distinguishing preserved runtime state from state that must restart, with evaluated-form/source/generated-origin identity. Show an unaffected artifact retained and affected artifacts rebuilt or rejected before reuse; reject a stale analysis/MIR/backend/runtime/package artifact, untracked build-affecting state and debug inspection outside grants/secret policy. Build-affecting session inputs are captured or explicitly nonhermetic; interactive manifests do not imply release runtime support. Build-affecting sessions emit transcripts, evaluated-form artifacts, syntax/core/MIR snapshots, dependency invalidation records and source maps; debug hooks cannot expose raw memory, host process state or model/tool outputs without grants. Source obligation `language/effects/interpret-tool-call`: Interpret a tool call against its declared schema, tool identity, human-review and authority policy, returning a typed result without ambient tool privilege. Accept: Interpret ai/tool-call through the declared tool identity and input/output schema, effects, capability and policy-required human review; validate and return a typed result with original effect/handler identity. Preserve actual external provider/account policy without introducing project work quotas. Reject: Reject schema/type mismatch, unknown tool, missing grant/review or ambient tool authority; a handler declaration cannot create authority. Required outputs: Typed tool-handler artifacts, schema validation, grant/review decisions, result/replay records and accepted/rejected fixtures. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Source obligation `language/effects/interpret-workflow-replay`: Interpret workflow event/replay operations and their time/random/activity/model/tool/review/retry/compensation records under the durable replay contract. Accept: Record workflow/event and workflow/replay operations with stable event/step identity, input/output schemas, effects, external results, time/random/activity/model/tool/review/retry/compensation decisions and replay IDs. Record mode writes and replay mode reads; concurrent branches replay deterministically with original handler labels/identity. Preserve R6 graph-declared replay-safe operations only where no R7/R8 recorded-output obligation applies. Reject: Reject missing/mismatched/reordered replay records, live nondeterministic work in recorded-output segments and silent repetition of external effects; emit L11-REPLAY-RACE when durable concurrency lacks a record. Required outputs: Typed handler/event/step graph, replay log, record-versus-replay traces, deterministic branch comparison and refusal diagnostics. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Source obligation `language/errors/emit-ai-policy-failure`: Emit structured audit/policy evidence for AI/model/tool/schema/defense/review failure instead of losing it in exception text. Accept: Emit structured policy/audit artifacts for model-provider failure, tool failure, schema validation, policy denial, prompt-defense trigger and human-review denial, preserving source spans and generated-origin chains. Actual external account/billing errors may remain explicit; removed project quotas are not restored. Reject: Reject free-text-only or missing AI/tool failure evidence, omitted policy/schema/review identity and lost source/generated origins; report L9-AI-ERROR. Required outputs: Typed AI/tool failure record, policy/audit/replay links, validation/denial fixtures and source-bound diagnostics. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime, effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Source obligation `language/errors/emit-durable-workflow-failure`: Emit and replay a durable workflow failure record with its step/input/error identity, retry/compensation policy and external-result/replay provenance. Accept: Persist and replay a workflow failure with step ID, input and output/error schemas, retry/compensation policy, time, external-call results and replay ID; retain source/generated origins and exercise failure plus compensation replay. Reject: Reject workflow failure without durable record, missing required schema/policy/result/replay identity or live re-execution during recorded replay; report L9-WORKFLOW-ERROR. Required outputs: Durable typed failure and compensation records, replay equality/refusal fixtures and source/generated-origin diagnostic artifacts. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Decision criterion `interface/language/effects/consume-recorded-action-result` (Open): In replay mode consume the matching typed recorded action/result event with exact identity, cardinality and order, returning the recorded value/failure without executing the external action again. Refuse: Reject missing, duplicate, out-of-order or mismatched recorded events and any live external repetition in a recorded-result segment. Required outputs: recorded-result consumption trace, exact replay result and identity/cardinality/order mismatch diagnostics. Dependencies consume auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks as typed operation artifacts, not whole-component completion. Preserve every source facet and unresolved metadata ID in the exact phase-09 decision allocation; no implementation acceptance is inferred. Decision criterion `interface/language/effects/perform-and-record-admitted-action` (Open): In live record mode perform the admitted action through its actual provider and append the typed action identity, result/failure and ordering event under the declared recording policy. Refuse: Reject execution without admission, missing/incorrect identity or ordering records and undeclared external effects; a supplied transcript or replayed result is not live action evidence. Required outputs: actual provider action/result and typed append-only record event tied to admission and source. Dependencies consume auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks as typed operation artifacts, not whole-component completion. Preserve every source facet and unresolved metadata ID in the exact phase-09 decision allocation; no implementation acceptance is inferred. Decision criterion interface/runtime/ai-memory-policy: At the selected AI memory/retrieval provider enforce source/trust/tenant namespace, schema and sink-taint policy, privacy, retention, deletion and embedding/provider identity. Emit memory read/write/retrieval/deletion decisions and replay identity; accept validated authorized access, reject cross-namespace/ungranted writes, expired retention, forbidden secret storage and unvalidated retrieved content at trusted sinks. Provider billing/account constraints remain external; project accounting cannot become an admission condition. Decision criterion interface/runtime/durable-effect-replay: Execute durable steps against versioned recorded inputs/outputs with workflow/step/event/effect/provider identity, idempotency and declared completion/transaction boundaries. Recorded-output segments consume matching records without reissuing external actions, rejecting missing/mismatched/order-inconsistent records; preserve retries, cancellation and compensation policy. R6 graph-declared replay-safe repetitions may execute only where no R7/R8 recorded-output obligation applies and authority still holds. Emit restart/replay equality and actual no-duplicate-effect traces; a replay-safe label cannot override required recorded behavior. Decision criterion interface/runtime/model-provider-execution: Invoke the declared model/provider through its typed prompt/message provenance, roles/digests, parameters/decoding settings, output schema and validation policy, preserving input taint, output validation, errors, source identity and replay/audit mode. Record actual provider/model substitution only when policy permits it. Accept an authorized validated response and reject wrong provider/model/decoding identity, prohibited substitution, missing validation/grant or live invocation in a required recorded-output segment; retain external billing policy without compiler work quotas. Decision criterion interface/runtime/nondeterminism-recording: For each admitted runtime action whose replay or audit policy requires recording, persist typed input/output digests, provider/action identity, error/retry decisions, timestamp source and source/generated origin; record scheduler decisions where replay depends on them. Emit actual record-mode traces and matching replay consumption, rejecting absent/mismatched identity/order/cardinality and silent live reexecution in recorded-output mode. Record-mode action and replay-mode consumption are conditional alternatives, not simultaneous mandatory effects; retain R6's authorized graph-declared repetition exception outside R7/R8 recorded-output obligations. Decision criterion interface/runtime/replay-compatible-upgrade: For a code/topology/schema or workflow-version upgrade, compare existing event histories, persisted state, actor snapshots and message versions against the new declared compatibility/migration/replay policy. Emit migration and replay evidence that existing histories remain usable; reject incompatible upgrades without such policy/evidence, schemaless state/messages and implicit rewriting of recorded external outcomes. Preserve idempotency, retry/cancellation/compensation and authority semantics across the admitted upgrade. Decision criterion interface/runtime/tool-provider-execution: Invoke the declared tool/provider with input/output schemas and validation, effect/side-effect class, caller grant intersected with the tool's own contract, timeout/retry/error mapping and required review/secret/taint policy. Emit actual invocation and policy/review decision records with replay identity; reject ungranted or out-of-contract effects, missing required review, invalid/tainted sink values, secret-policy violations and live calls in recorded-output segments. Prompt text, retrieved data and review records cannot create capability authority; preserve explicitly permitted alternatives for audit-only/interactive contexts. Decision criterion interface/schema/boundary-validation: At each external host/config/message/state/query/model/tool/memory/public-API boundary invoke the validator tied to the intended source schema/version and concrete trusted sink, preserving trust/taint, defaults/normalization, errors and origin. Emit validation and sink-admission outputs for valid values and reject wrong schema/version, invalid/missing fields or refinements, unsafe null/foreign representations, unvalidated taint and missing sink grants. Structural validation alone cannot authorize execution, deployment, mutation or secret disclosure; schema/compatibility/config-reload producers and runtime sink consumers remain separate. Preserve typed failure paths and secret-redacted diagnostics rather than host exceptions or silent coercion. Decision criterion interface/runtime/durable-failure-recovery: Execute the admitted durable step's declared timeout, retry, cancellation, failure mapping and required compensation, preserving workflow/step/event/provider/source and idempotency records through failure and recovery. Retain typed failure/recovery and compensation traces. Reject absent worker/job policy with DOM8-JOB and absent runtime failure contracts with their owning diagnostics; missing policy never authorizes retry, and non-idempotent retry decisions remain with Behavior A4. No attempt allowance is introduced. Source recovery preserves full owning clause context and requires independent current-composition review; implementation remains Open. Allocation interface/safety/safe8/workflow-replay (Open). Role: runtime owning producer or consuming-boundary checker. Input: task/shared-location/synchronization graph and selected target/provider memory model. Required positive predicate: Record nondeterminism, external calls, retry/signal/timer/idempotency and compensation/cancellation for workflow concurrency and reject unreplayable workflow actions. Positive output witness: Nondeterminism/external-call/retry/signal/timer/idempotency/compensation/cancellation replay records. Concrete negative case: Concurrent workflow behavior makes an unrecorded external call or replays a retry/timer/signal as a new side effect. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: workflow supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-safe-code-classification-and-taintunsafe-boundaries supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred."},
