     "- [ ] `runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/close-enforcement-and-observability-integration` Close enforcement and observability integration\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Capability runtime contract](../../docs/phase-08-runtime-architecture/122-r11-runtime-capability-enforcement-design.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Denial at actual service hook, redacted diagnostics and source-map preservation. R1/R11/R12: every authority-bearing action carries principal/package/deployment/artifact/source/effect/capability identity; deny by default and check both caller grant and tool/plugin contract; delegated handles are typed, scoped, provider-bound and revocable where supported, with use-after-revocation rejection; preserve grant/deny/delegate/revoke/audit records without secret disclosure and enforce deployment narrowing. Structured event/log/trace/metric/panic/replay bundles retain stable schemas/IDs, runtime/profile/target/source/generated-origin/artifact links, check/proof/replay references, redaction and remediation; sinks require grants, development services are marked, and sampling retains mandatory audit events without changing ordering, replay or safety. Reject ambient authority, ungranted sinks, secret/tainted/raw-memory leakage and lost required mappings/events. Dependencies: Auth supplies policy and grants, Lower supplies artifact/source maps, each runtime family supplies events, and testing/tooling/incident consumers validate bundles; these records do not grant authority or claim execution acceptance. P4: map actual lowered/generated host failures to Gravity source and generated origins where supported or required; record unavailable mappings honestly and reject missing required mappings. Compiler diagnostic emission alone is not this runtime consumer evidence. Criterion profile-gap/hosted/failure-source-mapping (Open): Input: Actual hosted runtime failure and emitted source/generated-origin mappings for the claimed runtime/version/host symbol and lowered artifact. Accept: Resolve the failure to Gravity source and generated-origin chains where supported or required; explicitly report unavailable mappings where conditional support permits. Reject: Missing required mapping, incorrect generated-origin chain and compiler diagnostic emission substituted for actual host-failure mapping evidence. Required outputs: Runtime source/diagnostic map and executed source-mapping fixture, P4-SOURCEMAP diagnostic with runtime/symbol/origin/policy context; unsupported optional mapping is recorded honestly. Dependencies: runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries, diag/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/preserve-primaryrelatedgenerated-origins-and-stable-order, emit/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/emit3-bind-provenance-to-bytes interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping hosted/failure-source-mapping; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion behavior/pkg6/runtime-permission-audit: accept For participating runtimes, record requested/granted/denied/used permission events with package/effect/capability/profile/target, grant source and policy identity in the declared audit schema. Reject A required use/denial event is missing, a runtime effect has no capability derivation or audit output discloses protected authority data. Emit Runtime permission audit records/schema linked to capability manifest and SBOM, with PKG6002 context for missing derivation. Dependencies: PKG6, R11, R12. Criterion `runtime/deployment-provider-authority/decision-interface` (Open): Input: Compiler-accepted effect/capability facts, package/deployment grants and actual deployment-specific provider identity, presence, scope, phase/lifetime and revocation state under the declared error/panic/audit policy. Outputs: Actual service-hook allow/deny/delegate/revoke records; Provider presence/scope and error/panic fixtures; Policy-required redacted telemetry/audit and source/identity diagnostics. Accept: At actual HTTP/GraphQL/migration and other applicable authority-bearing runtime boundaries, check provider presence and deployment narrowing plus caller/tool-contract grant scope and supported lifetime/revocation before the action. Preserve declared error/panic and required audit/telemetry behavior, source/generated origins and principal/package/deployment/artifact/effect/capability identity; keep secrets redacted. Conditional provider/family/source contexts remain conditional, not blanket new authority. Refuse: Missing/wrong-scope provider, undeclared/ungranted action, widened deployment authority or supported use after revocation; Missing policy-required audit/source mappings, secret leakage or ungranted observation sink; Compiler legality, Auth policy text or generated wrapper metadata substituted for actual runtime hook checks. Dependencies consume actual artifacts: Auth supplies typed policy/grants, compiler/Legality supplies accepted facts, Lower supplies emitted source/identity maps; Each applicable runtime/provider supplies actual hook results; S4/S5/S6 consumers preserve admission decisions and R12 consumers check required redacted records. Diagnostics: Applicable SAFE10/R11/R12 and S4/S5/S6 boundary diagnostics include provider/deployment/scope/effect/grant/source and declared error/panic/remediation without secret disclosure. These are required future products/results; no execution or implementation acceptance is claimed. Decision criterion interface/runtime/metadata-preservation: At every selected runtime/FFI/host/device/workflow boundary preserve original source and generated-origin edges, artifact/profile/target/provider identity, declared effects/grants, taint and required proof/replay/audit links into the emitted service event and diagnostic bundle. Emit successful cross-boundary round-trip evidence and reject lost/forged required origins, effects, taint, proof or event links. Where mapping support is conditional, record unavailable optional mappings honestly and reject missing required mappings; diagnostic publication alone is not the runtime consumer. Decision criterion interface/runtime/policy-safe-observation: Emit typed runtime log/trace/metric/audit and diagnostic bundles with stable event schema/ID, timestamp source, family/profile/target/artifact/provider identity, source/generated origins and relevant effect/capability/check/proof/replay links. Enforce sink/deployment grants and the full secret/credential/prompt/model/tainted/raw-memory/environment/package/database redaction policy, reporting redactions without values. Exercise allowed local logging and denied network telemetry, required audit-event retention under sampling and semantic/order/replay/safety equivalence with instrumentation; reject ungranted sinks, policy-forbidden disclosure and missing mandatory events. Mark development-only observability explicitly."},
