     "- [ ] `stdlib/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/reconcile-export-inventory-with-actual-callable-implementations` Reconcile export inventory with actual callable implementations\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Library source artifact](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/bootstrap_impl/components/foundation/00499-standard-library-source-artifact.clj)\n\nClosing evidence: Per-export source/implementation/fixture map, with absent exports explicitly open; compiled module manifests agree with package metadata, documentation and conformance discovery on namespace/artifact identity, callable exports, profiles, effects, capabilities, allocation, errors, safety and stability. Reject missing or inconsistent metadata, undeclared effects, missing grants, host-dependent core exports and unaudited unsafe internals with STD1001-STD1008 as applicable. Apply the source-specific acceptance and dependency matrix in plan.md. Source obligation `language/library/enforce-portability-layers`: Reject an upward dependency from a lower standard-library portability layer and report the exact namespaces shipped for the selected profile. Accept: Publish the L13 namespace-to-layer inventory for compiler core(0), portable data(1), memory/resources/concurrency(2), capability-backed host/platform(3) and domain/compiler libraries(4). Check actual dependency edges and emit the exact shipped namespace subset for each selected profile; higher-to-lower dependencies are permitted. Reject: Reject a lower-layer dependency on a higher layer, an undeclared namespace/layer or a profile manifest claiming an unavailable namespace; hosted-only convenience cannot silently define the lower layers. Required outputs: Source/actual layer and dependency graph, exact per-profile namespace availability manifest, allowed downward-edge and rejected upward-edge fixtures. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/execute-typed-graph-under-declared-build-effects, types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types4-preserve-and-invalidate-facts; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open. Decision criterion interface/language/library/publish-public-contract: Publish machine-readable namespace/operation contracts for profile/type/effect/capability, allocation/resource, error/panic, blocking/nondeterminism and stability semantics; bind them to actual exports. Reject: Reject missing/false export metadata, hidden host behavior, untracked authority and public declarations inconsistent with callable implementations. Required outputs: Versioned public API/export/profile manifests and contract-to-implementation conformance/denial evidence."},
