     "- [ ] `stdlib/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-resourceconcurrencyionetwork-apis` Complete resource/concurrency/IO/network APIs\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Module inventory](../../docs/phase-16-standard-library/README.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Provider-mediated executions, missing-grant rejection and safe resource teardown; STD6-STD9 fixtures exercise borrow/region escape, exactly-once close/transfer, child cancellation and lifetime, atomic memory order, forbidden blocking, root/symlink traversal, explicit text encoding, atomic-write durability failures, network timeout/retry/redirect/body/cancellation policy, TLS validation and secret redaction. Replay must record or isolate actual external effects and reject unrecorded nondeterminism; host delegation must preserve Gravity diagnostics and provider provenance. Runtime, Legality and Auth dependencies remain explicit in plan.md. Decision criterion interface/language/concurrency/enforce-structured-task-lifetime: Require each scoped spawned task to finish, cancel or explicitly transfer its handle before scope exit; retain scheduler and captured-owner/lifetime assumptions. Reject: Reject spawning without admitted scheduler support, orphan tasks, invalid borrow captures and scope exit without completion/cancel/transfer. Required outputs: Task parent/handle lifecycle ledger, cancellation cleanup/transfer traces and accepted/rejected structured-scope cases. Decision criterion interface/language/concurrency/execute-ordered-atomic: Execute atomic operations at declared legal target-supported memory order; default to sequential consistency unless a profile/library explicitly selects weaker order. Reject: Reject unsupported/illegal memory order, missing atomic alignment/scope or implicit weakening during lowering. Required outputs: Atomic operation/order/target manifest, default-order and explicit-weaker-order fixtures and unsupported-order diagnostics. Decision criterion interface/language/concurrency/send-typed-channel-message: Send a typed channel value through a legal ownership move or immutable copy, retaining sender/receiver lifetime and declared ordering/backpressure/cancellation policy. Reject: Reject type mismatch, mutable alias leakage, invalid ownership transfer and communication outside admitted scheduler/provider support. Required outputs: Typed channel schema, transfer/copy and lifetime trace, legal send and invalid-message/ownership refusals. Decision criterion interface/language/memory/allocate-provider-storage: Allocate through the explicitly selected family/provider with declared alignment/layout, initialization, failure/blocking, sharing and runtime/profile contract. Reject: Reject missing/incompatible providers, uninitialized safe reads, illegal alignment/layout and hidden allocation or sharing outside declared policy. Required outputs: Allocation/provider/layout/initialization records, failure and sharing fixtures and profile/ownership denial diagnostics. Decision criterion interface/domain/typed-service-handling: Execute typed service routes/handlers/jobs using declared request/response/error/auth/effect/grant and failure/idempotency contracts. Negative fixtures: Reject unvalidated request/response/error data, hidden handler effects, absent auth/grants and violations of declared idempotency/failure policy. Required outputs: Typed route/handler/job metadata and actual valid/invalid request, result and authority transcripts. Bind exact source/compiler/profile/target and actual API/provider/artifact identities; exercise accepted and rejected cases under the attached source conditions. Status Open; no execution acceptance is inferred. Decision criterion interface/stdlib/io/atomic-file-replacement: Perform claimed atomic file replacement under declared temporary-path, rename, flush and durability guarantees, exposing required evidence and failure behavior. Negative fixtures: Reject claiming atomicity/durability without temporary-path/rename/flush guarantees; expose platform failure and partial durability under the declared policy. Required outputs: Replacement/rename/flush/durability records and atomicity/failure fixtures. Bind exact source/compiler/profile/target and actual API/provider/artifact identities; exercise accepted and rejected cases under the attached source conditions. Status Open; no execution acceptance is inferred. Decision criterion interface/stdlib/io/read-text: Execute the documented filesystem text read using the supplied capability and in-root path while honoring explicit UTF-8 encoding and declared text-error policy. Negative fixtures: Reject missing filesystem capability, root escape, omitted encoding/error policy or silent lossy decoding. Required outputs: Actual in-root UTF-8 text-read results and missing-grant/path/decode diagnostics. Bind exact source/compiler/profile/target and actual API/provider/artifact identities; exercise accepted and rejected cases under the attached source conditions. Status Open; no execution acceptance is inferred. Decision criterion interface/stdlib/io/traversal-policy: Execute directory traversal under declared recursion, symlink, permission and cycle policy and reject root escape, symlink loops and platform-normalization gaps. Negative fixtures: Reject root escape, symlink loops, missing recursion/permission/cycle policy and platform-normalization gaps. Required outputs: Traversal results plus root/symlink/cycle/permission/platform refusal fixtures. Bind exact source/compiler/profile/target and actual API/provider/artifact identities; exercise accepted and rejected cases under the attached source conditions. Status Open; no execution acceptance is inferred. Decision criterion interface/stdlib/network/client-request: Execute actual client requests under the supplied network authority and declared timeout, retry/idempotency, redirect, body/schema/encoding, streaming, cancellation and replay policy. Negative fixtures: Reject undeclared hosts/ports or grants, policy-breaking retries/redirects/body/streaming/cancellation and unrecorded replay side effects. Required outputs: Actual request/response/error transcripts and timeout/idempotency/redirect/stream/cancel/replay policy fixtures. Bind exact source/compiler/profile/target and actual API/provider/artifact identities; exercise accepted and rejected cases under the attached source conditions. Status Open; no execution acceptance is inferred. Decision criterion interface/stdlib/network/tls-admission: Validate TLS trust roots and certificate policy, including pinning/expiry, rejecting disabled validation outside explicitly allowed unsafe or test contexts. Negative fixtures: Reject invalid/untrusted/expired or pin-mismatched certificates and disabled validation outside explicitly allowed unsafe/test contexts. Required outputs: Trust-root/certificate/pinning/expiry policy and accepted/refused TLS fixtures. Bind exact source/compiler/profile/target and actual API/provider/artifact identities; exercise accepted and rejected cases under the attached source conditions. Status Open; no execution acceptance is inferred."},
