     "- [ ] `stdlib/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/integrate-platform-modules-and-close-release-manifests` Integrate platform modules and close release manifests\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Platform outcome](../../docs/component-roadmaps/platform.md#release-outcome)\n\nClosing evidence: Actual supported platform API fixtures, unsafe audits and compatibility/stability report; STD16-STD17 fixtures distinguish target/build/runtime-host facts, all clock/random kinds, process command/args/environment/stdio/timeout/working-directory policy, MMIO widths/alignment/volatile ordering, interrupt effects/reentrancy, DMA ownership/coherence/completion and clock-domain synchronization. STD20 release evidence compares source, behavior, effects, capabilities, diagnostics, artifact schemas, profiles and fixtures; exercises experimental opt-in/internal-import denial, deprecation/replacement/removal schedules and governed breaking changes; and binds signed provenance to the actual release. Platform target and product-release outcomes retain their separate scope. Retain the STD20 per-release report/evidence assembly and exact release binding outcome. Reuse governance baseline/dimension comparison and PKG10/PKG12 provenance/signing producers as dependencies rather than reimplementing them. Every release still requires the appropriate compatibility and signed provenance reports; a compatibility classification or signature alone does not assemble those release-bound artifacts or confer governance approval. Reject the following false substitutes: A report can identify an incompatible change; its existence is not approval to release it. A valid signature over another artifact/release does not satisfy STD20008. A signed provenance record cannot replace old/new conformance comparison or the complete compatibility dimensions. STD17 library/device communication requires synchronization proof or checked adapters. For actual physical HDL crossings, the adapter must satisfy B9's source/destination clock/reset/latency/metastability and declared synchronizer/FIFO/handshake/proof or hardware-policy waiver rules. Software/device adapters and simulator APIs are not automatically physical HDL crossings; keep their checked-adapter outcome and capabilities distinct. Reject the following false substitutes: A clock-domain spelling or register declaration is not a synchronization check. A passing HDL CDC gate does not prove a standard device API invokes the checked adapter. A generic unsafe island is not a B9 hardware audit waiver, and a simulator does not confer live-device authority. Decision criterion interface/language/library/record-compatibility-event: Classify API/profile changes under semantic compatibility rules; breaking changes carry explicit migration and feasible shim records with source/version identity. Reject: Reject silent breaking changes, stale compatibility evidence and unchecked/semantics-changing shims; preserve justified infeasibility when no safe rewrite exists. Required outputs: Compatibility event/version record, migration/shim or infeasibility artifact and preserved/broken-client fixtures. Decision criterion interface/domain/typed-command-execution: Execute scripts/process/shell/file actions through typed argument/environment/root/path/command/quoting/taint/timeout/error/grant contracts. Negative fixtures: Reject missing command/argument/environment/root/working-directory/stdio/timeout/quoting/taint/error policy, root escape and ungranted process or shell effects. Required outputs: Typed command policy, actual result/exit/error transcripts, denied-grant and taint/path fixtures. Bind exact source/compiler/profile/target and actual API/provider/artifact identities; exercise accepted and rejected cases under the attached source conditions. Status Open; no execution acceptance is inferred. Decision criterion interface/stdlib/hardware/description-artifacts: Emit target-bound memory maps and interrupt tables from accepted hardware descriptions with declared register/handler constraints. Negative fixtures: Reject missing target/register/handler identity, invalid widths/alignment/ordering or memory-map/interrupt-table disagreement. Required outputs: Target-bound memory maps, interrupt tables and valid/invalid description checks. Bind exact source/compiler/profile/target and actual API/provider/artifact identities; exercise accepted and rejected cases under the attached source conditions. Status Open; no execution acceptance is inferred. Decision criterion interface/stdlib/hardware/timed-wait-policy: Require a declared clock source, physical bound and power policy on busy waits and timers. Negative fixtures: Reject omitted clock source, physical bound or power policy; compiler work quotas cannot substitute for target timing evidence. Required outputs: Declared clock/timer/busy-wait policy and physical-bound/power acceptance/refusal records. Bind exact source/compiler/profile/target and actual API/provider/artifact identities; exercise accepted and rejected cases under the attached source conditions. Status Open; no execution acceptance is inferred. Decision criterion interface/stdlib/platform/clock-kinds: Preserve declared wall, monotonic, CPU, compile-time and replay-recorded clock kinds rather than silently substituting one for another. Negative fixtures: Reject substituting wall/monotonic/CPU/compile-time/replay clocks, ambient ungranted reads and replay nondeterminism. Required outputs: Clock-kind/provider manifest and kind-distinction/grant/replay fixtures. Bind exact source/compiler/profile/target and actual API/provider/artifact identities; exercise accepted and rejected cases under the attached source conditions. Status Open; no execution acceptance is inferred. Decision criterion interface/stdlib/platform/target-host-fact-separation: Keep compilation target/build-host/runtime-host facts distinct and source target facts from compiler/package artifacts unless probing is explicitly requested. Negative fixtures: Reject build/runtime host facts substituted for compilation target facts or an undeclared live probe. Required outputs: Distinct target/build-host/runtime-host metadata bound to compiler/package artifacts. Bind exact source/compiler/profile/target and actual API/provider/artifact identities; exercise accepted and rejected cases under the attached source conditions. Status Open; no execution acceptance is inferred. Decision criterion interface/stdlib/stability/internal-import-denial: Reject user-package imports of internal library exports. Negative fixtures: Reject user-package import of an internal export even when a name is discoverable or the implementation exists. Required outputs: Export-stability metadata and user/internal import acceptance/denial fixtures. Bind exact source/compiler/profile/target and actual API/provider/artifact identities; exercise accepted and rejected cases under the attached source conditions. Status Open; no execution acceptance is inferred."},
