     "- [ ] `tools/finite-service-outcomes-and-remaining-work/lint-analysis-tool-maintainer` Lint / analysis-tool maintainer\n\nStatus: Open\n\nRemaining implementation tasks: Implement the contract rule classes against named compiler/manifest facts; add project-scoped baselines and rule explanations; implement checked fixes and structured export\n\nClosing evidence and governing contract: Rule source/facts and applicability visible? Unsafe fixes rejected? Baseline/fail-on-new reproducible? [Linter](../../docs/phase-13-tooling-and-developer-experience/180-t4-linter-specification.md) Require rule id/severity/inputs/fixability/profile/target and source/manifest spans; cover every T4 rule class, JSON/SARIF, baseline and rule-coverage artifacts, stable explain-rule output and combined source/manifest analysis. Reject unknown rules, unavailable facts, policy-forbidden stale spans, unchecked fixes and policy-blocking release findings. Foundation requirement gravity/canonical-concept-vocabulary: Publish the D3 reference meanings and relationships for profile, target, backend, runtime, effect, capability, safety outcome, artifact and file, and check representative compiler/package/runtime manifests against those meanings. Refusals: Reject a manifest that equates an effect with authority, a profile with a backend, or an artifact with its storage file; retain the offending span/field and owning concept reference. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Foundation requirement gravity/cross-phase-term-change-control: Before downstream reliance on a changed cross-phase concept, update the canonical D3 definition and affected contract/schema references together, record the compatibility decision and invalidate dependent terminology checks. Refusals: Reject use of a changed downstream meaning with an unchanged canonical definition, stale dependent checks or an unrecorded compatibility impact. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/bind-each-claimed-component-to-exact-implementation-and-conformance - Exact component/slice contracts, declared unsupported scope and claimed-support evidence. Foundation requirement gravity/domain-concept-layer-map: Publish a domain-concept map relating each declared concept to its source forms, Core/domain IR boundary, emitted artifact, effects and required capabilities; verify a representative domain product against that map. Refusals: Reject an unmapped claimed concept, a host API substituted for its source meaning or a mapping that treats an effect declaration as a capability grant. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products. Foundation requirement gravity/qualify-ambiguous-normative-terms: For normative uses whose meaning affects implementation, require an explicit qualified D3 concept or owning contract reference; report the exact ambiguous span and the competing interpretations. Refusals: Reject unqualified uses such as runtime/profile/target or effect/capability where they change the required implementation meaning; ordinary nonnormative prose does not create a new terminology gate. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Tooling decision interface/behavior/t4/fact-based-lint: Run declared rules against actual compiler/package/AI facts with identified inputs, applicable profile/target and stable structured diagnostic explanations. Required source-defined acceptance predicates (subject to their stated conditions): declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t4/1000-1025: - AI prompt/tool safety; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t4/1025-1060: - performance hints with evidence; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t4/1060-1090: - documentation completeness. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t4/1184-1282: - Lint diagnostics MUST include rule id, severity, source span or manifest path, and explanation. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t4/1282-1348: - Rules using compiler facts MUST name which facts they consumed. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t4/1549-1604: - Rules MUST declare profile and target applicability. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t4/1604-1678: - Package and artifact lints MUST operate on manifests as well as source. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t4/1678-1759: - AI and tool-safety lints MUST use taint, policy, prompt, and capability facts. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t4/1814-1883: - Rule docs MUST be available through `gravity lint --explain-rule`. ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t4/2220-2238: The linter emits: ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t4/2271-2288: - rule metadata; ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t4/2288-2330: - auto-fix patch artifact when requested; ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t4/2372-2396: - rule coverage report. ; negative-acceptance facet/ai-build-tools/t4/2694-2746: - Reject rule configurations with unknown rule ids. ; negative-acceptance facet/ai-build-tools/t4/2746-2850: - Reject baselines that hide diagnostics from changed source spans when policy forbids stale baselines. ; negative-acceptance facet/ai-build-tools/t4/2850-2927: - Reject lints that claim compiler facts unavailable for the current target. ; negative-acceptance facet/ai-build-tools/t4/2927-2994: - Reject release builds when policy maps lint severity to blocker. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t4/3011-3048: - `T4001` reports unknown lint rule. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t4/3123-3168: - `T4004` reports unavailable compiler fact. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t4/3209-3255: - `T4006` reports invalid rule configuration. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t4/3281-3340: - A lint report includes stable rule ids and source spans. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t4/3340-3395: - Baseline mode fails on newly introduced diagnostics. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t4/3448-3500: - Rule applicability changes by profile and target. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t4/3500-3563: - Package manifests and source files can be linted in one run. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t4/3563-3636: - AI safety lints detect untrusted prompt authority and overbroad tools. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t4/3636-3694: - Rule explanation output is stable and machine-readable. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t4/746-762: - syntax style; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t4/762-783: - namespace hygiene; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t4/783-806: - profile portability; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t4/806-827: - effect visibility; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t4/827-854: - capability minimization; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t4/854-883: - unsafe audit completeness; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t4/883-907: - FFI boundary hygiene; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t4/907-933: - taint and input safety; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t4/933-966: - package and dependency policy; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t4/966-1000: - artifact and provenance policy; Produce actual service evidence and owning rejection diagnostics for the applicable positive/negative cases; links, record flags and another service's success do not establish this behavior. Implementation remains Open. Tooling decision interface/behavior/t4/lint-baseline-policy: Apply the reproducible project rule configuration and fail-on-new/stale-baseline policy deterministically. Required source-defined acceptance predicates (subject to their stated conditions): declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t4/1430-1487: - Lints MUST support baselines and fail-on-new behavior. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t4/1487-1549: - Rule configuration MUST be project-scoped and reproducible. ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t4/2254-2271: - baseline file; ; negative-acceptance facet/ai-build-tools/t4/2694-2746: - Reject rule configurations with unknown rule ids. ; negative-acceptance facet/ai-build-tools/t4/2746-2850: - Reject baselines that hide diagnostics from changed source spans when policy forbids stale baselines. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t4/3048-3088: - `T4002` reports stale baseline entry. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t4/3209-3255: - `T4006` reports invalid rule configuration. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t4/3340-3395: - Baseline mode fails on newly introduced diagnostics. Produce actual service evidence and owning rejection diagnostics for the applicable positive/negative cases; links, record flags and another service's success do not establish this behavior. Implementation remains Open. Tooling decision interface/behavior/t4/lint-structured-export: Export the actual lint findings and source/rule identities as the declared JSON/SARIF artifacts. Required source-defined acceptance predicates (subject to their stated conditions): declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t4/1759-1814: - Lint output MUST support JSON and SARIF-like export. ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t4/2239-2254: - lint report; ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t4/2330-2372: - SARIF-like report for external systems; ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t4/2372-2396: - rule coverage report. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t4/3011-3048: - `T4001` reports unknown lint rule. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t4/3048-3088: - `T4002` reports stale baseline entry. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t4/3088-3123: - `T4003` reports unsafe auto-fix. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t4/3123-3168: - `T4004` reports unavailable compiler fact. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t4/3168-3209: - `T4005` reports release-blocking lint. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t4/3209-3255: - `T4006` reports invalid rule configuration. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t4/3281-3340: - A lint report includes stable rule ids and source spans. Produce actual service evidence and owning rejection diagnostics for the applicable positive/negative cases; links, record flags and another service's success do not establish this behavior. Implementation remains Open. Tooling decision interface/behavior/t4/validated-lint-fix: Apply an automatic lint fix only when it preserves semantics or passes the declared refactor validation. Required source-defined acceptance predicates (subject to their stated conditions): declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t4/1348-1430: - Auto-fixes MUST preserve reader output or be routed through refactoring checks. ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t4/2288-2330: - auto-fix patch artifact when requested; ; negative-acceptance facet/ai-build-tools/t4/2616-2694: - Reject lint auto-fixes that alter semantics without refactoring validation. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t4/3088-3123: - `T4003` reports unsafe auto-fix. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t4/3395-3448: - Auto-fix patches are validated before application. Produce actual service evidence and owning rejection diagnostics for the applicable positive/negative cases; links, record flags and another service's success do not establish this behavior. Implementation remains Open. D3 deprecated-term acceptance: Consume the governed terminology compatibility/deprecation record for each changed stable term, including its migration period and named replacement. Exercise old and replacement terms during that period and emit a stable source/manifest diagnostic naming the replacement; reject a missing migration period, premature removal or a diagnostic that omits the replacement. Preserve the affected schema, compiler/tool and package/governance references; the existing Release compatibility/change-control outcome owns the governed decision, and this Tools outcome checks and surfaces it."},
