     "- [ ] `tools/finite-service-outcomes-and-remaining-work/profile-performance-tool-maintainer` Profile / performance-tool maintainer\n\nStatus: Open\n\nRemaining implementation tasks: Capture real supported target samples; bind environment and source/artifact identity; report overhead, comparisons and safety-check evidence\n\nClosing evidence and governing contract: Samples measured rather than generated? Unavailable counters explicit? No unrelated grant or proofless elision? [Profiler](../../docs/phase-13-tooling-and-developer-experience/187-t11-profiler-and-performance-inspector-design.md) Verify benchmark/profile/target/artifact/environment/compiler and applicable device identity, source/MIR/sample links, measured or explicitly unknown overhead, structured trace/environment/comparison/regression/layout reports and policy thresholds. Separate model/tool latency, retry, replay and human-review time and actual external costs. Reject incompatible benchmark comparison unless policy permits normalization, unsupported counters, exceeded regression thresholds, missing check-elision evidence and unrelated grants. PERF5/D6/TEST12 benchmark producer: emit a machine-readable benchmark manifest with workload/dataset/seed, profile/target/artifact/source/compiler/backend/runtime/provider/dependency versions, input/layout, metric/units, warmup, samples, statistical method, variance/repeat policy, correctness/safety gates, threshold and harness. Capture hardware/features/OS/kernel/build/power/thermal fingerprint and counter source/support, raw samples, summary, baseline and attributable comparison/replay inputs. Cover core/numeric/dispatch/layout/FFI/concurrency/IO/GPU/workflow/compiler/build families; AI reports separately show model, tool, memory, human-review and replay latency/cost, preserving external billing. Reproduce historical measurements from stored identities; accept only compatible fingerprints/artifacts or explicitly reviewed normalization. Gate performance only after actual correctness/safety/precision/profile/replay checks, with proof for check-elision gains. Reject missing identity/metadata, unsupported counters, opaque AI totals, single-sample release gates and correctness-masking wins; emit PERF5/TEST12 structured diagnostics and accepted/rejected benchmark fixtures. PERF5/TEST12 baseline governance: deterministically classify no-regression, noise, environment drift, compiler/backend/runtime/provider/dependency regression, semantic/safety change and invalid baseline using explicit thresholds and variance/repeat policy. Fail threshold-exceeding comparisons unless accepted drift/intentional semantic policy applies; compare different artifacts or fingerprints only with approved normalization. Version the baseline registry and preserve benchmark/source/package/compiler/backend/environment/sample/threshold/review-owner/date history plus reviewed update record. Never hide correctness/safety failures by replacing a baseline. Exercise accepted reviewed updates and rejected unreviewed/stale baselines, noise, drift, incompatible normalization, threshold breaches and failed gates; emit regression decision, baseline diff/history and PERF5/TEST12 diagnostics containing benchmark/profile/target/metric/baseline/fingerprint/summary/threshold/gate state. PERF6 production-trace privacy: capture PGO summaries only under explicit access/retention/data policy; redact or aggregate tainted/secret-derived values, with governed raw-data handling only where policy permits. Emit privacy/redaction/aggregation/retention/access records linked to profile-data and public build artifact identities. Exercise actual capture/export consumers with user inputs, credentials/secrets, prompts, tool outputs and customer data; verify forbidden raw values never enter public artifacts, required redaction survives transformation and retention/access denials prevent the operation. Report violations as PERF6 privacy diagnostics with data/policy/workload/pass/profile/target and offending field; schema presence alone is insufficient. Tooling decision interface/behavior/t11/compatible-benchmark-comparison: Compare only declared compatible benchmark/metric contexts under the actual threshold/variance policy. Required source-defined acceptance predicates (subject to their stated conditions): declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t11/1364-1429: - Comparisons MUST use declared thresholds and benchmark policy. ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t11/2281-2315: - benchmark environment manifest; ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t11/2342-2363: - comparison report; ; negative-acceptance facet/ai-build-tools/t11/2733-2838: - Reject performance comparisons with different benchmark identities unless policy allows normalization. ; negative-acceptance facet/ai-build-tools/t11/3017-3077: - Reject CI regression passes when thresholds are exceeded. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t11/3211-3262: - `T11002` reports incompatible comparison inputs. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t11/3479-3537: - A benchmark run emits structured performance artifacts. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t11/3537-3581: - Comparison detects threshold regressions. Produce actual service evidence and owning rejection diagnostics for the applicable positive/negative cases; links, record flags and another service's success do not establish this behavior. Implementation remains Open. Tooling decision interface/behavior/t11/distributed-ai-cost-classes: Separate AI/distributed model or provider/tool latency, retry, replay and human-review time and applicable observed costs in performance reports. Required source-defined acceptance predicates (subject to their stated conditions): declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t11/1012-1043: - GC or runtime service costs; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t11/1568-1681: - AI and distributed performance reports MUST separate model/tool latency, retry, replay, and human-review time. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t11/3721-3800: - AI workflow reports separate provider, tool, replay, and human-review costs. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t11/976-1012: - model/tool cost for AI workflows; Produce actual service evidence and owning rejection diagnostics for the applicable positive/negative cases; links, record flags and another service's success do not establish this behavior. Implementation remains Open. Tooling decision interface/behavior/t11/performance-artifact: Emit structured reproducible profiling reports bound to their measurement inputs without acquiring unrelated program authority. Required source-defined acceptance predicates (subject to their stated conditions): declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t11/1755-1842: - Performance artifacts MUST be structured and reproducible enough for trend tracking. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t11/1842-1909: - Profiling MUST not require granting unrelated runtime authority. ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t11/2259-2281: - performance report; ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t11/2342-2363: - comparison report; ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t11/2386-2410: - check elision report; ; negative-acceptance facet/ai-build-tools/t11/2838-2915: - Reject reports missing profile, target, artifact, or environment identity. ; negative-acceptance facet/ai-build-tools/t11/3077-3139: - Reject profiling sessions requiring unrelated capabilities. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t11/3156-3211: - `T11001` reports missing performance identity field. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t11/3211-3262: - `T11002` reports incompatible comparison inputs. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t11/3262-3313: - `T11003` reports missing check-elision evidence. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t11/3313-3360: - `T11004` reports unsupported target counter. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t11/3360-3403: - `T11005` reports performance regression. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t11/3403-3453: - `T11006` reports profiler capability overreach. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t11/3479-3537: - A benchmark run emits structured performance artifacts. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t11/3581-3664: - Reports link measurements to source, MIR, or artifact positions where available. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t11/3874-3943: - Profiling does not grant authority outside declared runtime needs. Produce actual service evidence and owning rejection diagnostics for the applicable positive/negative cases; links, record flags and another service's success do not establish this behavior. Implementation remains Open. Tooling decision interface/behavior/t11/performance-proof-view: Link performance claims about check elimination or transforms to their actual preserved proof/checker evidence. Required source-defined acceptance predicates (subject to their stated conditions): declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t11/1043-1070: - check elision decisions; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t11/1429-1496: - Safety check elision views MUST show proof or analysis evidence. ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t11/2386-2410: - check elision report; ; negative-acceptance facet/ai-build-tools/t11/2915-2963: - Reject check-elision claims with no evidence. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t11/3262-3313: - `T11003` reports missing check-elision evidence. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t11/3664-3721: - Check elision output cites proof or analysis evidence. Produce actual service evidence and owning rejection diagnostics for the applicable positive/negative cases; links, record flags and another service's success do not establish this behavior. Implementation remains Open. Tooling decision interface/behavior/t11/profile-measurement-identity: Measure actual target execution with exact subject/compiler/runtime/environment/device/source identity, disclosing instrumentation overhead and unavailable counters. Required source-defined acceptance predicates (subject to their stated conditions): declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t11/1070-1107: - specialization and layout choices. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t11/1172-1276: - Profiling runs MUST identify profile, target, artifact, benchmark, environment, and compiler version. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t11/1276-1364: - Performance reports MUST link samples to source or artifact positions where possible. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t11/1496-1568: - Runtime overhead from profiling MUST be measured or declared unknown. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t11/1681-1755: - Hardware, firmware, and GPU reports MUST record target device identity. ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t11/2238-2258: The profiler emits: ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t11/2281-2315: - benchmark environment manifest; ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t11/2315-2342: - sample or trace records; ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t11/2363-2386: - regression decision; ; artifact-schema facet/ai-build-tools/t11/2410-2449: - layout and specialization summaries. ; negative-acceptance facet/ai-build-tools/t11/2838-2915: - Reject reports missing profile, target, artifact, or environment identity. ; negative-acceptance facet/ai-build-tools/t11/2963-3017: - Reject target counters used on unsupported targets. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t11/3156-3211: - `T11001` reports missing performance identity field. ; diagnostic facet/ai-build-tools/t11/3313-3360: - `T11004` reports unsupported target counter. ; acceptance-fixture facet/ai-build-tools/t11/3800-3874: - Unsupported counters are rejected for targets that cannot provide them. ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t11/792-818: - wall time and CPU time; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t11/818-849: - allocation counts and bytes; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t11/849-894: - cache and branch counters where available; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t11/894-917: - latency percentiles; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t11/917-931: - throughput; ; declaration-or-behavior-contract facet/ai-build-tools/t11/931-976: - energy or device counters where supported; Produce actual service evidence and owning rejection diagnostics for the applicable positive/negative cases; links, record flags and another service's success do not establish this behavior. Implementation remains Open."},
